WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:02.102
Joe: A Brit and an American swap countries

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:03.970
to try each other's McDonald's.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.438
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:09.576
We'll start with some things
you can find in the UK

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:11.478
but I think might be
slightly different over here.

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:13.713
Let's start with the
iconic McDonald's Big Mac.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:17.183
So, I mean, visually,
looks pretty much the same.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:19.519
You've got the quite
sad, flimsy beef patties.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:20.787
Let's give it a try.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:24.024
So, I think there are some
subtle differences there,

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:25.892
actually. Like, broadly speaking,

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:28.428
if you gave it to me and were
like, "This is a UK Big Mac,"

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:30.463
I don't think I would doubt you.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:33.333
I think it's the sauce,
because the UK Big Mac sauce

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:37.470
has got quite a tang to it,
almost, and this is very gentle.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.671
I barely get anything from it.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:41.741
The Big Mac. Now, this
looks exactly like a Big Mac

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:42.909
anywhere in the world.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:45.445
You know what I gotta do. Oop and oop.

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:46.813
Now let's give this a shot.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.316
If that isn't exactly
the same, it's close.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.118
I mean, if I could do one side
by side I'd probably notice,

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:55.055
but I do not taste any difference.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:57.090
I remember when we did
"Fast-Food Chemistry,"

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.092
you guys had more
chemicals and stuff to use,

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:00.226
but I'm here to say

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.362
the chemicals have not
made a striking difference.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:04.064
It tastes almost exactly the same.

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:06.633
Then we're on to the fries and
the Coke aspect of the meal.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:09.269
Firstly, I have to point
out how enormous these are.

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:10.904
The size of this drink is ridiculous.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:11.738
This is way bigger

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:14.674
than almost any fast-food
drink I've seen in the UK ever.

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:17.243
Even the fries as well.
This box of fries is huge.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.578
They've kind of sunk down a little bit,

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.914
so it doesn't really show how full it was.

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.715
But this carton is massive.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.417
You can fit so many fries in here.

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.386
It feels like almost double the size

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.021
of a carton of UK fries.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.389
I mean, these are pretty good.

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:31.691
I will say, I think they've
held up a lot better

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.259
after a bit of time out of the fryer

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.327
than UK fries have.

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.129
UK McDonald's fries, I think maybe

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.964
because they don't have
as many ingredients,

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:39.999
there aren't the preservative
chemicals in there,

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.534
they don't really hold
up very well at all.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:42.469
As soon as they come out the fryer,

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:44.170
they kind of just get
worse and worse and worse.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.172
So you have to eat them
really while they're hot.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.574
I think taste-wise,

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:49.476
there are some slight differences as well.

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:53.713
There is something more than
just salt going on here.

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:54.948
So, I only know this because we made

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:58.351
that "Fast-Food Chemistry"
episode of McDonald's fries,

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:01.654
but there is a sort of
artificial-beef flavor

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:04.491
that's added to these, and
you do kind of taste it.

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:06.526
It's very subtle, but there's a kind of

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:08.995
savory depth of flavor to these

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:11.431
that you just don't get in the UK.

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:13.366
I kind of like it. I can't lie.

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:14.734
My first thing about these fries,

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:17.437
these guys are pale looking.

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:19.706
Not the bright yellow I'm
used to in the States.

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:22.742
The whole thing is just potato,
salt, and oil, that's it?

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:29.482
Yeah, and I believe it,
because these are bland.

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.650
Man!

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.484
What?

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:35.288
Mm-mm, no on the fries.
USA ones are way better.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:37.757
And then finally, this
enormous McDonald's Coke.

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:40.894
I don't know what it is
about McDonald's Coke,

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.262
but it just always hits different.

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:43.563
That happens in the UK

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:45.331
and, yeah, kind of still happens here.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.332
Another iconic menu item

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:48.902
that I thought was worth
trying was McNuggets.

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:51.037
So, just visually speaking,
before I even try it,

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:53.439
these look quite different
to British McNuggets.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:56.075
I'm fairly sure the ones
in the UK are deep-fried.

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:57.877
Correct me if I'm wrong, editor.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:01.681
But these ones look almost
more deep-fried somehow,

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:04.050
just in terms of the way that the breading

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.452
has kind of puffed up and
blistered a little bit.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:07.287
I will say, I think the breading

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:09.189
maybe has slightly more seasoning,

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:11.424
a bit more flavor going
on here than I'm used to.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:13.860
The chicken itself I think
is pretty much the same.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.262
I think I might prefer
British nuggets. Sorry, guys.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:19.332
Nuggets look like almost
exactly the same size,

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:23.102
smell the same, same amount
of crispness on the skin.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:27.874
No, much blander. Much blander.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.909
You guys are getting a terrible deal

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:32.078
with these nuggets, because this is dry.

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:33.947
I did notice it says
"100% chicken breast meat"

00:03:33.947 --> 00:03:35.181
on this one.

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:36.749
I do not know if that's
the case in America.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.585
Can we get that on-screen?

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:39.953
But I've just been informed, no,

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:42.355
of the chicken that they use,

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.958
100% of it is chicken breast meat,

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:47.493
but it's only 45% chicken, right?

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.896
It says "100% chicken breast" on it.

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:52.832
The implication there is that
the chicken is 100% chicken,

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:55.068
or it's 100% chicken meat.

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:57.170
It is not. Deceptive!

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.171
The last thing we wanted to compare

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:00.974
in both countries was the McCrispy.

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:02.842
Here is an American McCrispy.

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:05.845
It looks fairly similar
to ours on the surface.

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:08.848
This one I think is a
potato roll rather than

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:10.984
the more pretzel-y brioche version

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:12.085
that you find in the UK.

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:13.753
There's no sauce.

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:16.756
It's just pickles and
a fried chicken patty.

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:17.957
I really like the pickles.

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:20.960
I think pickles and fried
chicken is a great combination,

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.862
and it's not super common in the UK.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:24.264
I will say, I think it needs a sauce.

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:27.066
I think technically they claim
that they butter the rolls

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:29.969
and that butter is I
guess therefore the sauce,

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:31.537
but it's kind of dry.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:33.306
The chicken's just a
little bit thin as well.

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.041
I feel like the McCrispy
in the UK tends to be

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:37.844
a thicker and slightly
juicier piece of chicken.

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:42.181
This is a fairly thin and
quite dry chicken breast.

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:43.483
The McCrispy.

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:44.317
Harry: Yellow box.

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:46.619
Oh, nice! All right.

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.721
I'm pleasantly surprised by the bun.

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.990
It reminds me of King's Hawaiian rolls.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.558
Yeah, this looks like our McChicken.

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:54.394
It is so close to the McChicken.

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:57.096
Better bun than the McChicken,

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:58.631
but the crispiness of the chicken patty.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:04:59.632
It tastes slightly different.

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:01.234
I would say the McChicken sauce is,

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:03.303
I hate to say it, is a bit sweeter.

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:04.237
Because I love the McChicken.

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:06.105
Like, the taste of that is in my DNA.

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:09.676
Here are all the US menu items

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:11.611
you won't find at a UK McDonald's.

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:13.646
Here's all the UK McDonald's menu items

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.248
I can't get in the US.

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:16.683
We'll start with some chicken options,

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:19.619
namely the deluxe McCrispy

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:21.721
and the spicy deluxe McCrispy.

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.890
Let's take a look at the deluxe McCrispy

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:26.659
and see what exactly they're
adding to make it deluxe.

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:29.562
The roll looks pretty much the
same as the standard version.

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:31.230
The chicken looks the same.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.066
But I think when they say deluxe,

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:36.502
that just means they've added
mayo, lettuce, and tomato.

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.137
I don't know if that is enough

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:39.839
to qualify something as deluxe.

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:41.541
Doesn't seem super deluxe to me.

00:05:41.541 --> 00:05:44.711
I also think that tomato is
just a bad topping for a burger.

00:05:44.711 --> 00:05:46.713
They've kind of made this
worse, in my opinion.

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:48.448
I'm going to take a bite
of the spicy one and see

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:49.982
if it's good and if it's spicy.

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:52.385
It does have some heat to
it. They weren't kidding.

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:55.154
For my measly British-person palate.

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:57.724
I think I would probably
just buy the regular version

00:05:57.724 --> 00:06:00.660
of the McCrispy and then
add some sauce to it.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:04.130
So, you got a bacon mayo
chicken and a mayo chicken.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:07.367
No, this might be exactly
what the McChicken's like.

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:09.235
Nah, it's a little wimpier.

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:11.471
Yeah. Is this what you're talking about?

00:06:11.471 --> 00:06:14.374
Like, it's a big McNugget? Yeah.

00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:19.379
The mayo's weird. Has a
really stale aftertaste.

00:06:19.379 --> 00:06:22.281
I'm telling you, your guys'
breaded chicken at McDonald's

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:24.517
has no flavor compared
to the one in the US.

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:27.820
The McCrispy was crispier,
had more flavor in the sauce,

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.088
and the bun was nicer.

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:31.190
Yeah, this is a bummer.

00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:34.460
Ugh, we got the same with
bacon. Do I really have to ...

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:35.661
No.

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:38.798
Look at how flimsy your bacon is.

00:06:38.798 --> 00:06:40.199
Now we're on to some beef options,

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:42.135
starting with the McDouble.

00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:44.404
I have just some kind
of existential questions

00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:45.471
about the McDouble.

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:47.774
Namely, why does it exist?

00:06:47.774 --> 00:06:49.208
Because we have the double cheeseburger.

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:50.476
Let's give it try.

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:53.279
I'm genuinely curious,
like, how is this different

00:06:53.279 --> 00:06:55.948
to just a double cheeseburger, Joe?

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:57.583
One slice of cheese. Joe
says one slice of cheese.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:58.418
Talk me through it.

00:06:58.418 --> 00:07:00.787
OK, so what's going on
here is that the McDouble

00:07:00.787 --> 00:07:02.422
has one slice of cheese in between,

00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:04.657
where with double cheese, we
have two slices of cheese.

00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:05.725
I think that's the only difference.

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:06.993
I honestly think it's, right,

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:09.095
because this is just, like,
the standard McDonald's.

00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:09.929
Yeah, this looks very normal.

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:11.731
Right? It's just one less slice of cheese

00:07:11.731 --> 00:07:13.900
from what we can tell. And
the price difference is,

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:15.768
let's get that on-screen.

00:07:15.768 --> 00:07:18.337
So if you want to save
that amount of money,

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:20.473
get yourself a McDouble

00:07:20.473 --> 00:07:23.409
and pass the savings on to you.

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:25.678
There you go. Cheers, Joe.
You heard it here first.

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:28.347
Next up we have the Quarter
Pounder with cheese deluxe.

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:31.684
So, similarly to the McCrispy,

00:07:31.684 --> 00:07:33.986
they've turned this thing
into a deluxe burger

00:07:33.986 --> 00:07:38.424
by just adding some lettuce,
some mayo, and some tomato.

00:07:38.424 --> 00:07:39.492
You know what they've tried to do here?

00:07:39.492 --> 00:07:41.260
They've tried to just make a Whopper.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.563
This is the double Quarter
Pounder with bacon.

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:47.433
Now this is a burger.

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:50.136
This one does what you would
expect a Quarter Pounder to do.

00:07:50.136 --> 00:07:52.171
It's just loads of meat and cheese.

00:07:52.171 --> 00:07:53.706
I want to talk more
about this bacon as well,

00:07:53.706 --> 00:07:54.841
because this bacon's good.

00:07:54.841 --> 00:07:56.909
One thing that I think we
do quite badly in the UK

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:58.711
at fast food is bacon.

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:01.747
A lot of the bacon you'll
find on UK restaurants

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:04.317
is this very pallid pink color,

00:08:04.317 --> 00:08:06.486
whereas this one, stronger flavor,

00:08:06.486 --> 00:08:07.987
you get some smokiness from it.

00:08:07.987 --> 00:08:09.722
The bacon on this is way better,

00:08:09.722 --> 00:08:12.358
and therefore that makes
it a very enjoyable burger.

00:08:12.358 --> 00:08:14.927
Yes, I think the deluxe
should just be more beef

00:08:14.927 --> 00:08:17.029
and some bacon rather than vegetables

00:08:17.029 --> 00:08:18.331
that no one wants to eat. Come on.

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:21.601
Oh, yeah, now we're talking. Two patties.

00:08:21.601 --> 00:08:23.836
Although, I'm telling you
guys, the patty on patty

00:08:23.836 --> 00:08:25.638
with nothing in the middle is just weird.

00:08:25.638 --> 00:08:28.975
A poppy-sesame-seed-bun hybrid?

00:08:28.975 --> 00:08:31.143
Whoa!

00:08:31.143 --> 00:08:32.945
Yeah, it doesn't look like barbecue sauce.

00:08:32.945 --> 00:08:35.147
Barbecue sauce is, like, an amber brown.

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:36.282
Eh.

00:08:36.282 --> 00:08:38.351
I think the bacon kind of screws it up

00:08:38.351 --> 00:08:40.253
because your bacon is so flimsy.

00:08:40.253 --> 00:08:42.188
I think this would work
with American bacon,

00:08:42.188 --> 00:08:45.157
because American bacon would
just be, like, crisp —

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:46.659
I mean, it's not like
it has to be crispier.

00:08:46.659 --> 00:08:49.862
It's just, this is really rubbery.

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:52.632
What do you guys think barbecue sauce is?

00:08:52.632 --> 00:08:53.966
Bacon double cheeseburger.

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:55.601
I'm not impressed with
your bacon here, guys.

00:08:55.601 --> 00:08:56.569
I'm not impressed.

00:08:56.569 --> 00:08:59.372
Look. Look at ...

00:08:59.372 --> 00:09:01.474
everyone in America,
look how weird this is.

00:09:03.109 --> 00:09:04.010
Yeah, like ...

00:09:05.011 --> 00:09:06.512
I'm pretty sure we had a
bacon double cheeseburger

00:09:06.512 --> 00:09:08.748
at some point at McDonald's,
and it wasn't like this.

00:09:08.748 --> 00:09:12.652
Our bacon is crispier, more
dispersed evenly, I guess.

00:09:12.652 --> 00:09:14.954
Just have two strips going
right through the middle here.

00:09:14.954 --> 00:09:17.557
That's a disaster. It's a total disaster!

00:09:17.557 --> 00:09:19.392
All right, McPlant. Harry, get in here

00:09:19.392 --> 00:09:21.460
and explain to me what
I'm doing, what this is.

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:24.196
This is the McPlant. It's
McDonald's fake-meat burger.

00:09:24.196 --> 00:09:25.898
It took them ages to develop this.

00:09:25.898 --> 00:09:27.533
They tested it in Scandinavia first.

00:09:27.533 --> 00:09:29.101
It was available in Sweden for a while.

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:31.237
They also developed their own vegan cheese

00:09:31.237 --> 00:09:33.205
because McDonald's couldn't
find a commercial vegan cheese

00:09:33.205 --> 00:09:34.040
that they thought was good enough.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:36.475
Yeah, I believe it. Look at
this. This looks terrifying.

00:09:36.475 --> 00:09:37.310
I'll leave you to it, buddy.

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:38.778
Thanks, bud. What he said.

00:09:38.778 --> 00:09:41.847
I think it was only available
in a few places in the US.

00:09:41.847 --> 00:09:43.883
Came and went.

00:09:43.883 --> 00:09:45.518
So, at least the US audience,

00:09:45.518 --> 00:09:47.219
not impressed with the McPlant.

00:09:48.888 --> 00:09:50.756
Yeah, that's not good.

00:09:50.756 --> 00:09:53.492
There is definitely some
plant-based meat that tastes good,

00:09:53.492 --> 00:09:54.827
that tastes like meat.

00:09:54.827 --> 00:09:55.661
This ain't it.

00:09:55.661 --> 00:09:59.031
I want to take this moment
to try your UK Coca-Cola.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.602
Man, the Coke here is way better.

00:10:02.602 --> 00:10:03.836
You guys make it with real sugar.

00:10:03.836 --> 00:10:06.505
F--- off with this!

00:10:06.505 --> 00:10:07.607
Does this ... ?

00:10:07.607 --> 00:10:09.241
And these are the dippers, right?

00:10:10.409 --> 00:10:13.112
Who do you think you are, McDonald's?

00:10:13.112 --> 00:10:15.147
Who do you think you are, doing this?

00:10:15.147 --> 00:10:17.850
You just took the dippers and put them ...

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:19.185
Oh, God, gross!

00:10:19.185 --> 00:10:21.253
What is this, like ... what is this?

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:25.157
Vegetables.

00:10:26.058 --> 00:10:27.827
Yo, this sucks ass, dude.

00:10:27.827 --> 00:10:29.996
Yeah, the vegetarian says he loves them.

00:10:29.996 --> 00:10:31.063
Put a asterisk next to that.

00:10:31.063 --> 00:10:33.199
Of all the things he
can eat at McDonald's,

00:10:33.199 --> 00:10:34.300
there's two, right?

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:36.669
And this is one of them. So OK, great.

00:10:36.669 --> 00:10:38.404
I never want this.

00:10:39.438 --> 00:10:40.940
Moving on.

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:42.074
Ah, Chicken Selects.

00:10:42.074 --> 00:10:44.577
This is closer to what our McChicken

00:10:44.577 --> 00:10:45.978
and our nuggets taste like.

00:10:48.581 --> 00:10:49.649
Oh, yeah.

00:10:49.649 --> 00:10:51.684
Damn, wish we had this in America.

00:10:51.684 --> 00:10:53.753
The sour cream and chive
dip is really good.

00:10:53.753 --> 00:10:55.521
Here are all the
exclusive wraps and salads

00:10:55.521 --> 00:10:58.124
that you can find in the US
that you won't find in the UK.

00:10:58.124 --> 00:11:00.159
That's not a mistake. There
are just none of them.

00:11:00.159 --> 00:11:01.460
It's not even that there's no exclusives.

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:03.696
There's just no wraps
or salads, full stop,

00:11:03.696 --> 00:11:05.431
on a US McDonald's menu.

00:11:05.431 --> 00:11:08.034
Joe: USA!

00:11:08.034 --> 00:11:10.202
I can't exactly say that
the UK salads are good

00:11:10.202 --> 00:11:12.071
at McDonald's, but at least
we have them, you know?

00:11:12.071 --> 00:11:14.674
You have an option if you
somehow are trying to eat healthy

00:11:14.674 --> 00:11:16.542
but have ended up in a McDonald's anyway.

00:11:16.542 --> 00:11:18.611
Whereas in America the closest
thing you have to a salad

00:11:18.611 --> 00:11:20.813
is this bag of apple slices.

00:11:20.813 --> 00:11:24.183
Oh, my God. I hate wraps.

00:11:24.183 --> 00:11:27.987
This is a really smart way
of presenting this. A pita.

00:11:27.987 --> 00:11:29.188
Isn't that a pita?

00:11:29.188 --> 00:11:31.123
Harry: Tortilla, isn't it?

00:11:31.123 --> 00:11:33.292
Oh, yeah. I guess it's
closer to a tortilla.

00:11:33.292 --> 00:11:35.861
Leon: Also, the way you say it.

00:11:35.861 --> 00:11:36.796
Joe: "Peed-a."
Leon: Yeah.

00:11:36.796 --> 00:11:37.630
How do you say it?

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:38.464
Leon: "Pit-ta."

00:11:38.464 --> 00:11:41.100
No, that's wrong. It's
with an I. "Peed-a."

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:42.034
Charlie: I would say "pit-ta."

00:11:42.034 --> 00:11:43.235
Well, you'd be wrong.

00:11:48.407 --> 00:11:49.775
Ugh, what kind of dressing is this?

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:54.246
Well, it says garlic, but
it's not very garlicky.

00:11:54.246 --> 00:11:58.250
OK, so then we have the
grilled version of this. Yeah.

00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.819
No, no, no, no, no.

00:12:02.788 --> 00:12:05.925
What flavor could this possibly have?

00:12:05.925 --> 00:12:07.960
Oh, come on.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:09.328
Charlie: I thought that
was a bit of bread!

00:12:09.328 --> 00:12:10.896
No.

00:12:10.896 --> 00:12:14.200
Oh, man. That has no flavor.

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:17.503
Yeah, you can get a grilled-
or crispy-chicken salad,

00:12:17.503 --> 00:12:18.537
but we didn't get them

00:12:18.537 --> 00:12:21.774
because I didn't fly across
the planet to eat a salad.

00:12:21.774 --> 00:12:24.710
Hey, this is fun. Nacho cheese wedges.

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:27.346
Well, we're much further from Mexico,

00:12:27.346 --> 00:12:29.782
so how good could the
nacho cheese actually be?

00:12:31.717 --> 00:12:32.852
Not bad.

00:12:32.852 --> 00:12:36.088
It's certainly the most
flavorful thing I've eaten today.

00:12:36.088 --> 00:12:37.590
Now it's time for the
exclusive condiments,

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:38.958
and you know what that means.

00:12:38.958 --> 00:12:41.994
S-s-s-s-s-s-sauce talk.

00:12:43.295 --> 00:12:46.732
The very first sauce
talk, "Foreign Exchange."

00:12:46.732 --> 00:12:48.567
Sauce talk.

00:12:48.567 --> 00:12:51.003
We're going to start with
this one, spicy Buffalo.

00:12:52.304 --> 00:12:53.873
Yeah, so I think that's
the same one that they put

00:12:53.873 --> 00:12:55.608
on the spicy McCrispy.

00:12:55.608 --> 00:12:57.910
It's pretty good. It's basically
like if you take a mayo

00:12:57.910 --> 00:12:59.311
and just pour some Frank's RedHot in it.

00:12:59.311 --> 00:13:01.013
Let's try the honey mustard out.

00:13:01.013 --> 00:13:02.948
I personally love a honey mustard.

00:13:03.983 --> 00:13:05.851
You certainly get the
honey. It's pretty good.

00:13:05.851 --> 00:13:09.388
I think the balance of that
is more on the honey side,

00:13:09.388 --> 00:13:11.791
and it needs to swing slightly
more to the mustard side.

00:13:11.791 --> 00:13:13.459
Now, this one I'm excited for.

00:13:13.459 --> 00:13:17.196
It's ranch. We call it
"rahnch," not ranch.

00:13:18.898 --> 00:13:20.666
Yeah, that's pretty good.

00:13:20.666 --> 00:13:23.936
Yeah, it's got a sort of herby tang to it.

00:13:23.936 --> 00:13:24.970
Then we've got a couple of condiments

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:26.639
which are technically breakfast items

00:13:26.639 --> 00:13:28.340
but we're going to count
under sauce talk anyway.

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:31.310
We'll start with the mild picante salsa.

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:33.012
I think this is supposed to be paired

00:13:33.012 --> 00:13:36.482
with the breakfast burrito,
which we will get onto later.

00:13:36.482 --> 00:13:37.850
But I'm going to try it with a nugget.

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:39.084
Joe: Oh, Jesus.

00:13:40.386 --> 00:13:42.054
OK, that's enough.

00:13:42.054 --> 00:13:42.888
Just do it.

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:46.292
Does what it says on the tin.

00:13:46.292 --> 00:13:48.828
That's just a mild salsa, really.

00:13:48.828 --> 00:13:50.095
Also on the breakfast-condiments list,

00:13:50.095 --> 00:13:52.231
we have hotcake syrup.

00:13:52.231 --> 00:13:54.066
I guess, like, maybe
legally they're not allowed

00:13:54.066 --> 00:13:57.303
to call it maple syrup, so hotcake syrup.

00:13:57.303 --> 00:14:00.306
I mean, people eat pancakes
with bacon and maple syrup,

00:14:00.306 --> 00:14:03.542
so why can't chicken nuggets
and maple syrup go together?

00:14:03.542 --> 00:14:06.212
OK, I thought I'd invented
something special there,

00:14:06.212 --> 00:14:09.081
but nope, turns out I cannot claim

00:14:09.081 --> 00:14:10.816
that combination as my own.

00:14:10.816 --> 00:14:12.484
It's butter.

00:14:12.484 --> 00:14:13.652
They have butter on the menu.

00:14:13.652 --> 00:14:17.356
I think, again, designed to
be used with the hotcakes.

00:14:17.356 --> 00:14:20.860
The final condiment
option is some grape jam.

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:22.628
I will say, we don't tend to have many

00:14:22.628 --> 00:14:25.097
grape-flavored products in
the UK for whatever reason.

00:14:28.834 --> 00:14:30.936
Mm.
Joe: Yeah?

00:14:30.936 --> 00:14:32.571
It's pretty tasty.

00:14:32.571 --> 00:14:33.939
Maybe not in combination with the chicken,

00:14:33.939 --> 00:14:35.507
but the grape jam is quite nice.

00:14:35.507 --> 00:14:37.443
Already, your ketchup, it's bizarre.

00:14:37.443 --> 00:14:41.247
It makes sense why this would be ketchup,

00:14:41.247 --> 00:14:42.915
considering what ketchup is.

00:14:42.915 --> 00:14:45.384
But American ketchup is way sweeter.

00:14:45.384 --> 00:14:46.619
I don't know if that's a
good thing or a bad thing,

00:14:46.619 --> 00:14:48.687
but I'm eating that, and I'm like,

00:14:48.687 --> 00:14:49.688
if that was on a plate,

00:14:49.688 --> 00:14:51.290
I was eating somewhere
that that was on a plate

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:52.625
and I was dipping into it,

00:14:52.625 --> 00:14:54.193
I'd be like, "Oh, what sauce is this?"

00:14:54.193 --> 00:14:55.427
Because I wouldn't think that's ketchup.

00:14:55.427 --> 00:14:57.263
Like, "Oh, it's this fun
tomato sauce you got."

00:14:57.263 --> 00:14:58.797
I wouldn't go, "Oh, ketchup."

00:14:58.797 --> 00:15:00.299
Yeah, it's that different.

00:15:00.299 --> 00:15:03.168
OK, the barbecue sauce, from
the country with no barbecue.

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:07.773
Let's see what you guys
think barbecue is. Nope.

00:15:07.773 --> 00:15:09.475
I don't know what this is supposed to be.

00:15:09.475 --> 00:15:11.577
Sweet chili dip. Here we go.

00:15:11.577 --> 00:15:13.379
Better. Just OK.

00:15:13.379 --> 00:15:15.781
McDonald's barbecue sauce is its own

00:15:15.781 --> 00:15:18.751
special brand of barbecue sauce.

00:15:18.751 --> 00:15:20.819
Yeah, this is pretty close to it, but

00:15:20.819 --> 00:15:23.856
this one's a little more mustardy.

00:15:23.856 --> 00:15:26.191
So, OK. Yeah, it's not bad.

00:15:26.191 --> 00:15:29.161
All right, sweet and sour.
Ooh, that's really good.

00:15:29.161 --> 00:15:33.799
Oh, hell yeah, dude. Sweet
curry. Been waiting for this.

00:15:33.799 --> 00:15:34.767
That's really good!

00:15:34.767 --> 00:15:35.801
We don't have any exclusive options

00:15:35.801 --> 00:15:37.436
when it comes to the
food inside a Happy Meal,

00:15:37.436 --> 00:15:38.737
but I did want to get one and just kind of

00:15:38.737 --> 00:15:41.707
see what the vibe was, see
what the toy is, crucially.

00:15:41.707 --> 00:15:43.776
So, at the time of recording this,

00:15:43.776 --> 00:15:45.511
"The Little Mermaid"
hit theaters recently,

00:15:45.511 --> 00:15:48.480
so they seem to be doing a
collab with "The Little Mermaid."

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:50.683
Does that mean I'm going to
get a "Little Mermaid" toy?

00:15:50.683 --> 00:15:51.817
Let's find out.

00:15:54.119 --> 00:15:56.488
So, we get — oh, these fries are so cute.

00:15:56.488 --> 00:15:59.892
So, this is a UK large. [Joe laughing]

00:15:59.892 --> 00:16:01.393
This is what I'm used to.

00:16:01.393 --> 00:16:04.363
I will say, in the UK, the
fries come in a paper bag

00:16:04.363 --> 00:16:05.898
rather than one of these

00:16:05.898 --> 00:16:08.667
simply adorable little cartons,

00:16:08.667 --> 00:16:10.703
which, honestly, huge fan of.

00:16:10.703 --> 00:16:12.738
I went for the McNuggets,

00:16:12.738 --> 00:16:15.507
which tend to come in a box of four.

00:16:15.507 --> 00:16:17.309
Ah, there you go. You get
the apple slices within that.

00:16:17.309 --> 00:16:19.478
This is the American salad.

00:16:19.478 --> 00:16:21.780
And, of course, we get a toy.

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:24.083
Oh, it's King Triton! Let's go!

00:16:24.083 --> 00:16:27.453
"Place your toy on a phone
or tablet for more fun,"

00:16:27.453 --> 00:16:29.588
which I do think we have
to try and do real quick.

00:16:29.588 --> 00:16:30.823
OK, try again. OK, put it down.

00:16:30.823 --> 00:16:32.324
Put my phone on the desk.

00:16:32.324 --> 00:16:33.926
You guys are getting this, right?

00:16:33.926 --> 00:16:35.461
Getting all of this? This is crucial.

00:16:35.461 --> 00:16:38.397
Place your toy on there. Pick a thing.

00:16:38.397 --> 00:16:39.431
I'll just go there.

00:16:39.431 --> 00:16:40.499
OK. Play the game.

00:16:40.499 --> 00:16:42.067
"Turn your sound on."

00:16:42.067 --> 00:16:46.038
[water swooshing]

00:16:46.038 --> 00:16:48.941
I'm going to be honest. This is a miss.

00:16:48.941 --> 00:16:51.543
Some kind of pattern? "Learn pattern."

00:16:53.012 --> 00:16:54.380
That one, that one.

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:56.015
[water swooshing]

00:16:56.015 --> 00:16:57.649
Did it. I win.

00:16:57.649 --> 00:16:59.985
DC Happy Meal.

00:16:59.985 --> 00:17:03.288
I've been told that it's —
one second. We got the toy.

00:17:03.288 --> 00:17:07.159
Oh, Poison Ivy. Fast-food
fish is way more popular here.

00:17:07.159 --> 00:17:11.063
You guys love your fast fish. I do not.

00:17:11.063 --> 00:17:12.297
It smells fishy.

00:17:17.036 --> 00:17:17.870
For the first time,

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:20.372
your food being flavorless
is a good thing.

00:17:20.372 --> 00:17:21.607
Fries. Yeah, actually,

00:17:21.607 --> 00:17:23.809
I would say this is also our kids size.

00:17:23.809 --> 00:17:25.144
Let's take a look at the Poison Ivy toy.

00:17:25.144 --> 00:17:27.346
What the hell? What is — OK.

00:17:27.346 --> 00:17:28.781
Oh, there's something inside.

00:17:30.115 --> 00:17:33.052
Ah, stickers, a game.

00:17:33.052 --> 00:17:35.154
All right. Fun for kids.

00:17:35.154 --> 00:17:37.122
Now we're on to some
McCafé and dessert options.

00:17:37.122 --> 00:17:38.857
Unfortunately, I couldn't
get a few of these,

00:17:38.857 --> 00:17:40.592
but here are the ones that
I was able to find today.

00:17:40.592 --> 00:17:42.294
We'll start with a good
old-fashioned American

00:17:42.294 --> 00:17:44.163
chocolate chip cookie.
This looks pretty good.

00:17:44.163 --> 00:17:45.564
We're kind of bad at cookies in the UK.

00:17:45.564 --> 00:17:47.599
I don't know what it
is, but they tend to be

00:17:47.599 --> 00:17:51.003
very dry and crumbly
rather than soft and chewy.

00:17:52.704 --> 00:17:53.539
That's not bad.

00:17:53.539 --> 00:17:55.240
What's more American than apple pie?

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:58.377
I'll tell you what, an
apple pie from McDonald's.

00:17:58.377 --> 00:18:01.280
This is the American McDonald's apple pie.

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:04.083
In the UK, a McDonald's apple
pie is actually deep-fried.

00:18:04.083 --> 00:18:05.184
It just looks very different.

00:18:05.184 --> 00:18:06.685
This is a baked apple pie,

00:18:06.685 --> 00:18:08.253
so you get more of a lattice going on.

00:18:08.253 --> 00:18:09.888
You see the filling there, but it's baked,

00:18:09.888 --> 00:18:12.624
so I guess they don't need
to seal it on every side

00:18:12.624 --> 00:18:13.592
because it's not going in a fryer.

00:18:13.592 --> 00:18:15.260
It's not all going to
spill out into the oil.

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:16.929
I don't know if it's
going to hold up or not.

00:18:18.230 --> 00:18:21.033
I think the UK might be
doing better apple pies

00:18:21.033 --> 00:18:23.502
than the US is, at least
when it comes to McDonald's.

00:18:23.502 --> 00:18:25.270
The pastry's fine.

00:18:25.270 --> 00:18:26.805
The filling tastes pretty much identical

00:18:26.805 --> 00:18:29.208
to the filling of a UK apple pie.

00:18:29.208 --> 00:18:30.943
But yeah, like, the baked pastry

00:18:30.943 --> 00:18:32.544
is just not the same as fried pastry.

00:18:32.544 --> 00:18:34.480
And then there's actually
another pie option

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:36.415
on the menu right now at a US McDonald's.

00:18:36.415 --> 00:18:38.317
This one is a strawberry cream pie.

00:18:39.218 --> 00:18:40.352
That's pretty good.

00:18:40.352 --> 00:18:42.054
As I said, there were
some desserts and pastries

00:18:42.054 --> 00:18:44.490
that we weren't able to
get today. Here they are.

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:47.493
In the UK, you can also
get exclusive McFlurries.

00:18:47.493 --> 00:18:48.994
Could not get them because,
you're not going to believe it,

00:18:48.994 --> 00:18:51.330
but the ice cream machines
are also broken in the UK.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:53.732
You can get yourself a Maltesers McFlurry

00:18:53.732 --> 00:18:55.467
and a Smarties McFlurry.

00:18:55.467 --> 00:18:59.071
OK, we got the McCafé snacks.

00:18:59.071 --> 00:19:00.372
First up, oh, a doughnut.

00:19:00.372 --> 00:19:01.440
Hey, who doesn't like a doughnut?

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:03.475
Ooh, yo!

00:19:03.475 --> 00:19:05.911
This one is covered in
sugar. Look at that.

00:19:05.911 --> 00:19:09.615
Muffin. Berry. Berry muffin.

00:19:09.615 --> 00:19:11.283
A millionaire's doughnut, huh?

00:19:13.118 --> 00:19:15.521
Ooh, with the cream inside?

00:19:15.521 --> 00:19:16.588
It is pretty decadent.

00:19:16.588 --> 00:19:17.923
I don't know if I feel like a millionaire.

00:19:17.923 --> 00:19:19.024
I don't think millionaires
are eating those,

00:19:19.024 --> 00:19:20.459
I'm going to be honest with you.

00:19:20.459 --> 00:19:22.594
Oh, hell yeah. Oh, yeah.

00:19:22.594 --> 00:19:23.695
Yep. That's a good cookie.

00:19:23.695 --> 00:19:24.863
Let's talk about the drinks.

00:19:24.863 --> 00:19:26.765
First of all, there are
some hot and cold coffees

00:19:26.765 --> 00:19:28.300
which are available in both countries.

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:30.269
It does seem like the US
actually has a bigger range

00:19:30.269 --> 00:19:32.938
of coffees, particularly when
it comes to the iced versions,

00:19:32.938 --> 00:19:34.973
while in the UK we're limited
to a couple of basic ones

00:19:34.973 --> 00:19:37.009
like an iced latte. Over
here you can get all sorts.

00:19:37.009 --> 00:19:39.811
You can get things like
your iced caramel mocha,

00:19:39.811 --> 00:19:43.715
your frappa mochaccino,
Dunkin' thingymajiggy.

00:19:43.715 --> 00:19:44.583
You know the ones.

00:19:44.583 --> 00:19:46.318
There are some interesting
non-coffee drinks though

00:19:46.318 --> 00:19:47.886
that I do want to try and talk about now.

00:19:47.886 --> 00:19:49.221
We're going to start with
this one down the end,

00:19:49.221 --> 00:19:51.023
which I believe is Hawaiian Punch.

00:19:52.624 --> 00:19:54.493
Not common in the UK at all.

00:19:57.596 --> 00:19:58.797
Joe: [laughs] Yep.

00:19:58.797 --> 00:20:00.532
OK.

00:20:00.532 --> 00:20:01.466
If this is the first one,

00:20:01.466 --> 00:20:03.502
I think I have a bit
of a storm coming here.

00:20:03.502 --> 00:20:05.537
It's pretty good, but, wow, is that sweet.

00:20:05.537 --> 00:20:08.440
This one is an American-style lemonade.

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:09.841
As I've said before in the show,

00:20:09.841 --> 00:20:11.877
lemonade in the UK is like Sprite.

00:20:11.877 --> 00:20:14.780
It's, like, a clear,
carbonated lemony beverage,

00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:17.482
whereas this looks like
a good old-fashioned

00:20:17.482 --> 00:20:19.451
American lemonade.

00:20:19.451 --> 00:20:21.286
It's not bad. It's weird to me

00:20:21.286 --> 00:20:22.888
that lemonade isn't carbonated,

00:20:22.888 --> 00:20:25.090
but that's pretty good. That's
actually fairly refreshing,

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:27.226
unlike maybe the Hawaiian Punch was.

00:20:27.226 --> 00:20:30.596
Also, happy birthday, Grimace,
while we're on the subject.

00:20:30.596 --> 00:20:32.664
They did have a special Grimace shake,

00:20:32.664 --> 00:20:34.933
but the ice cream machine was broken

00:20:34.933 --> 00:20:37.002
at the McDonald's that
we went to, of course,

00:20:37.002 --> 00:20:38.270
so I haven't been able
to get the Grimace shake,

00:20:38.270 --> 00:20:39.104
which I'm really sad about.

00:20:39.104 --> 00:20:41.206
Here's what it's supposed to look like.

00:20:41.206 --> 00:20:43.375
They do not have a good
old-fashioned cup of tea

00:20:43.375 --> 00:20:45.244
on the menu at an American McDonald's.

00:20:45.244 --> 00:20:47.346
What they do have is sweet tea.

00:20:47.346 --> 00:20:48.914
I felt like I had to try it as a Brit.

00:20:48.914 --> 00:20:51.583
You know, I have to give my
thoughts on everyone's teas.

00:20:52.451 --> 00:20:55.420
Aah.
Joe: [laughs] No!

00:20:55.420 --> 00:20:58.156
They weren't kidding when
they called it sweet tea.

00:20:58.156 --> 00:21:01.560
So, this was supposed to be a
blue-raspberry frozen Fanta,

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:03.295
and this was supposed to be a frozen Coke.

00:21:03.295 --> 00:21:06.598
However, now it is just a
melted blue-raspberry Fanta

00:21:06.598 --> 00:21:09.034
and a melted Coke,
otherwise known as Coke.

00:21:10.269 --> 00:21:12.771
Ooh. That's pretty good.

00:21:13.972 --> 00:21:15.974
Yeah, just tastes like Coke.

00:21:15.974 --> 00:21:19.111
It does somehow, like, still
has a bit of fizz to it,

00:21:19.111 --> 00:21:20.646
and the same with the Fanta, actually.

00:21:20.646 --> 00:21:23.849
I do think I would like
these if they were frozen.

00:21:23.849 --> 00:21:25.651
I think on a really hot day, for example,

00:21:25.651 --> 00:21:27.486
carrying a frozen Coke
around sounds delightful.

00:21:27.486 --> 00:21:31.323
So, yeah, would quite like
those on the UK menu, maybe.

00:21:31.323 --> 00:21:35.127
Then we have a, what I
believe to be, Hi-C drink,

00:21:35.127 --> 00:21:37.829
Hi-C Orange Lavaburst.

00:21:37.829 --> 00:21:41.199
Yeah, so this isn't carbonated,
and it's not fruit juice.

00:21:41.199 --> 00:21:43.135
It's somewhere in the middle.

00:21:43.135 --> 00:21:46.538
I'd put it reasonably close to an Oasis

00:21:46.538 --> 00:21:47.806
that we can get in the UK,

00:21:47.806 --> 00:21:50.609
which is also a sort of
non-carbonated fruity beverage.

00:21:50.609 --> 00:21:51.476
I don't love it.

00:21:51.476 --> 00:21:54.980
Last but by no means least,
we have milk on the menu.

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:56.715
I think this is kind of aimed at kids.

00:21:56.715 --> 00:22:01.019
I never want to meet a
person who is a grown adult

00:22:01.019 --> 00:22:03.322
and goes to McDonald's and
orders milk with their meal.

00:22:03.322 --> 00:22:04.756
These are all the exclusive
drinks we got today.

00:22:04.756 --> 00:22:06.658
There are some other
ones, and here they are.

00:22:06.658 --> 00:22:09.061
All right, the McCafé exclusives.

00:22:09.061 --> 00:22:11.096
They didn't label any of
them, so I'll just guess.

00:22:11.096 --> 00:22:12.731
That's definitely hot
chocolate, but let's see,

00:22:12.731 --> 00:22:14.766
how does it compare to the deluxe?

00:22:14.766 --> 00:22:15.867
Mm-mm.

00:22:16.802 --> 00:22:18.070
Oh, this is that butter
thing. That's terrible.

00:22:18.070 --> 00:22:20.005
We'll get back to that. Let me
find the other hot chocolate.

00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:22.507
That's a hot chocolate.

00:22:24.109 --> 00:22:25.010
I can't tell the difference.

00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:27.612
I don't know which one's
deluxe. Would deluxe be size?

00:22:27.612 --> 00:22:30.382
Wait, this one has that
buttery oil floating in it.

00:22:30.382 --> 00:22:33.452
And this, I know what this is.

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:35.754
Tea!

00:22:38.357 --> 00:22:40.959
I don't get it. I don't
get why this is so popular.

00:22:40.959 --> 00:22:42.427
The McCafé food's pretty good. I like it.

00:22:42.427 --> 00:22:45.163
You got a good selection
here. The drinks, not so much.

00:22:45.163 --> 00:22:47.265
I like banana, I like
banana-flavored stuff,

00:22:47.265 --> 00:22:50.135
and we don't nearly have as
much in the United States.

00:22:50.135 --> 00:22:54.473
This tastes exactly like a
banana Laffy Taffy. It's great.

00:22:54.473 --> 00:22:56.241
What's Oasis?

00:22:56.241 --> 00:22:57.542
Yeah, no, thanks.

00:22:57.542 --> 00:23:00.345
I mean, it's sweet, but
it reminds me of Gatorade.

00:23:00.345 --> 00:23:01.680
Orange juice. I know what
orange juice tastes like.

00:23:01.680 --> 00:23:05.317
What is this? Robinsons Fruit Shoot.

00:23:05.317 --> 00:23:07.419
Why is it a Fruit Shoot?
What's the shooting part?

00:23:07.419 --> 00:23:08.520
Leon: It's for kids, really.

00:23:08.520 --> 00:23:09.955
Oh, so it's just, like,
shoot it in my mouth,

00:23:09.955 --> 00:23:11.390
like, "aah"? That what it's for?

00:23:11.390 --> 00:23:13.658
Leon: I think it's called that
because kids are more likely

00:23:13.658 --> 00:23:15.060
to be like, "Yeah, give me a Fruit Shoot."

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:15.994
Than what?

00:23:15.994 --> 00:23:17.763
Leon: Than, like, "Give me a Coke."

00:23:17.763 --> 00:23:20.332
I would like to know why
this is called Fruit Shoot.

00:23:20.332 --> 00:23:22.033
OK, so I think it's called,
I haven't looked it up,

00:23:22.033 --> 00:23:23.268
I think it's called Fruit
Shoot because it wants you

00:23:23.268 --> 00:23:25.504
to squeeze, like, shoot it
in your mouth, like, "blah!"

00:23:26.838 --> 00:23:28.540
And Leon thinks it's because

00:23:28.540 --> 00:23:30.809
it sounds better than saying Coke.

00:23:30.809 --> 00:23:32.244
Now we're going to talk
about the most important meal

00:23:32.244 --> 00:23:33.311
of the day, breakfast.

00:23:33.311 --> 00:23:35.781
We'll start with this one,
the steak and egg McMuffin.

00:23:35.781 --> 00:23:39.451
That doesn't really look,
taste, or feel like a steak.

00:23:39.451 --> 00:23:42.521
Now, next up, America has some
breakfast biscuit options.

00:23:42.521 --> 00:23:43.622
So, from what I've seen,

00:23:43.622 --> 00:23:45.991
a biscuit looks very much like a scone,

00:23:45.991 --> 00:23:48.360
which is obviously a classic British dish.

00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:51.263
Now, the fact that they would
be putting breakfast food,

00:23:51.263 --> 00:23:53.098
like bacon, eggs, sausages,

00:23:53.098 --> 00:23:56.401
into what is effectively
a scone is weird to me

00:23:56.401 --> 00:23:58.236
and I think will be weird
to a lot of Brits as well.

00:23:58.236 --> 00:24:00.772
So, this is just a
classic sausage biscuit.

00:24:00.772 --> 00:24:03.408
It does look pretty like a scone.

00:24:03.408 --> 00:24:05.811
It's maybe a bit more,
like, smooth on the outside

00:24:05.811 --> 00:24:06.978
than I'm expecting from a scone.

00:24:08.613 --> 00:24:10.315
So dry.

00:24:10.315 --> 00:24:11.516
Joe: Told you.
Harry: Oh, my God.

00:24:11.516 --> 00:24:12.484
Hey, Joe from "Food Wars" here.

00:24:12.484 --> 00:24:14.319
I just wanted to say, that's not a scone.

00:24:14.319 --> 00:24:15.420
It's a different biscuit.

00:24:15.420 --> 00:24:16.922
I don't know what he's talking about.

00:24:16.922 --> 00:24:18.290
He'll be chewing on that
for the next four minutes,

00:24:18.290 --> 00:24:19.424
but it's different.

00:24:19.424 --> 00:24:20.525
He's right. It's different.

00:24:20.525 --> 00:24:22.527
It's not a scone. It's somehow worse.

00:24:22.527 --> 00:24:23.595
Yeah, apparently I chose badly

00:24:23.595 --> 00:24:24.896
with the sausage being my first one,

00:24:24.896 --> 00:24:26.665
because that was dry as a desert.

00:24:26.665 --> 00:24:29.301
So let's have a quick bite
of a bacon, egg, and cheese,

00:24:29.301 --> 00:24:32.437
which is a classic American-slash-New
York breakfast combo.

00:24:33.572 --> 00:24:34.906
It's still pretty dry, but the addition

00:24:34.906 --> 00:24:36.308
of the other stuff definitely helps.

00:24:36.308 --> 00:24:38.410
What are the takeaways there?

00:24:38.410 --> 00:24:41.613
Scones and biscuits are
different, not the same.

00:24:41.613 --> 00:24:44.049
A scone is a little bit more crumbly,

00:24:44.049 --> 00:24:46.218
generally slightly sweeter.

00:24:46.218 --> 00:24:50.322
These are not sweet.
Slightly more bready texture.

00:24:50.322 --> 00:24:53.358
I'm still not convinced by
the notion of them as, like,

00:24:53.358 --> 00:24:54.793
the foundation of a breakfast sandwich,

00:24:54.793 --> 00:24:56.828
just mostly because of how dry they are.

00:24:56.828 --> 00:24:59.264
But, hey, who am I to
judge American culture?

00:24:59.264 --> 00:25:00.198
Now, these I'm excited for.

00:25:00.198 --> 00:25:01.666
I've heard very good things
about these from Joe.

00:25:01.666 --> 00:25:03.835
These are McDonald's McGriddles.

00:25:03.835 --> 00:25:06.271
If I remember correctly
from watching Joe eat these,

00:25:06.271 --> 00:25:11.076
they've got pancakes that
they sort of inject with syrup

00:25:11.076 --> 00:25:13.845
and then use those as the
buns for a breakfast sandwich,

00:25:13.845 --> 00:25:15.680
which sounds pretty excellent.

00:25:15.680 --> 00:25:18.383
I'll try the bacon, egg, and
cheese. See how we get on.

00:25:19.951 --> 00:25:21.853
Still slightly dry, but way less dry

00:25:21.853 --> 00:25:23.522
than the biscuit, and very tasty.

00:25:23.522 --> 00:25:24.956
I'm going to go even more syrup,

00:25:24.956 --> 00:25:27.125
because what's better
than adding more syrup

00:25:27.125 --> 00:25:30.161
to something which is
already full of syrup?

00:25:30.161 --> 00:25:35.000
McGriddles, yes. Biscuits, not so sure.

00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:36.701
So, this was the bacon,
egg, and cheese McGriddle.

00:25:36.701 --> 00:25:38.737
You can also get McGriddles with sausage,

00:25:38.737 --> 00:25:41.306
sausage and egg and cheese, or the steak,

00:25:41.306 --> 00:25:42.674
which I will not be trying.

00:25:42.674 --> 00:25:44.009
The next exclusive breakfast item

00:25:44.009 --> 00:25:47.279
is the bacon, egg, and
cheese breakfast bagel.

00:25:47.279 --> 00:25:50.482
We used to have bagels on the
menu at the UK McDonald's,

00:25:50.482 --> 00:25:51.950
and they were wonderful.

00:25:51.950 --> 00:25:53.318
Part of the breakfast menu,

00:25:53.318 --> 00:25:56.588
toasted bagels with your choice
of toppings and fillings,

00:25:56.588 --> 00:25:57.522
really good.

00:25:57.522 --> 00:25:59.791
Pandemic hit, they cut them from the menu,

00:25:59.791 --> 00:26:01.159
and they've not returned.

00:26:01.159 --> 00:26:03.228
And personally, I'm furious about that.

00:26:06.031 --> 00:26:08.266
Yeah. I've missed you so much, bagel.

00:26:08.266 --> 00:26:10.435
Next up, we have a sausage burrito.

00:26:10.435 --> 00:26:13.171
Breakfast burrito is really
not a thing in the UK.

00:26:13.171 --> 00:26:15.807
We're just generally bad at Mexican food.

00:26:15.807 --> 00:26:17.309
This is obviously designed to be enjoyed

00:26:17.309 --> 00:26:18.777
with the mild salsa.

00:26:18.777 --> 00:26:19.945
It's actually pretty good.

00:26:19.945 --> 00:26:21.713
And then lastly on the
breakfast menu, we have these,

00:26:21.713 --> 00:26:23.114
the Big Breakfasts.

00:26:23.114 --> 00:26:28.119
The standard Big Breakfast
is a slab of scrambled egg,

00:26:28.119 --> 00:26:29.821
a sausage patty, and a biscuit.

00:26:29.821 --> 00:26:32.223
And this is the Big
Breakfast with hotcakes,

00:26:32.223 --> 00:26:34.492
which is the egg, biscuit, and sausage

00:26:34.492 --> 00:26:36.661
but then also comes with two pancakes.

00:26:36.661 --> 00:26:38.663
Both of these come with dips,
including a little thing

00:26:38.663 --> 00:26:41.700
of whipped butter and, of
course, the hotcake syrup.

00:26:41.700 --> 00:26:42.968
So, I wasn't sure what the difference was

00:26:42.968 --> 00:26:45.270
between pancakes and hotcakes.

00:26:45.270 --> 00:26:47.872
Joe's just done a quick
Google, and apparently,

00:26:47.872 --> 00:26:51.076
hotcakes tend to be a bit
thicker and denser than pancakes.

00:26:51.076 --> 00:26:53.244
I mean, to me, that just
tastes like a pancake.

00:26:53.244 --> 00:26:55.814
I'm thinking maybe they've
just called them hotcakes

00:26:55.814 --> 00:26:57.182
to make them sound more
fancy or different,

00:26:57.182 --> 00:26:59.017
but, yeah, not bad.

00:26:59.017 --> 00:27:02.387
And, of course, McDonald's
UK, I gotta try the breakfast.

00:27:02.387 --> 00:27:06.257
All right, first up,
the mini potato waffles,

00:27:06.257 --> 00:27:07.726
hash browns that are shaped like a waffle.

00:27:07.726 --> 00:27:09.494
I don't know why this specific shape.

00:27:11.963 --> 00:27:12.998
Yeah, dude.

00:27:12.998 --> 00:27:14.966
For some reason, it tastes
a lot better in waffle form.

00:27:14.966 --> 00:27:16.735
I don't know why that is.
These are really good.

00:27:16.735 --> 00:27:19.137
What do we got here? Breakfast sandwich.

00:27:19.137 --> 00:27:23.008
This is the bacon roll with brown sauce.

00:27:23.008 --> 00:27:25.477
It's like a hamburger bun! Look at this.

00:27:26.311 --> 00:27:27.979
There's your brown sauce right there.

00:27:27.979 --> 00:27:30.248
Hm. Eh.

00:27:30.248 --> 00:27:33.284
It's just OK. Nothing special. It's bland.

00:27:34.552 --> 00:27:36.254
I'm starting to think that you in the UK,

00:27:36.254 --> 00:27:38.590
you guys don't like, your
stuff isn't as, like,

00:27:38.590 --> 00:27:41.226
intense as ours in America is.

00:27:41.226 --> 00:27:44.896
Like, this wouldn't fly
in the US because it's not

00:27:44.896 --> 00:27:47.766
dripping with cheese and
doesn't have an egg in it

00:27:47.766 --> 00:27:49.768
and the buns aren't, like, über-buttery.

00:27:50.702 --> 00:27:52.170
It's just too plain. It's too boring.

00:27:52.170 --> 00:27:53.738
This is the same thing with just ketchup.

00:27:56.307 --> 00:27:57.976
Aw.

00:27:57.976 --> 00:28:00.645
Now we're getting more in my speed.

00:28:00.645 --> 00:28:03.114
This one has cheese and
bacon in it. Oh, yeah.

00:28:03.114 --> 00:28:04.649
Is that sausage?

00:28:04.649 --> 00:28:05.817
Yeah, this looks more like something

00:28:05.817 --> 00:28:07.952
that you'd get in the US.

00:28:07.952 --> 00:28:11.256
Yeah. Cheesy flatbread, oh, God.

00:28:13.291 --> 00:28:16.661
Cheesy — oh, come on, guys.
Yeah, see, this is the bacon.

00:28:16.661 --> 00:28:18.063
This is more like the bacon we're used to.

00:28:18.063 --> 00:28:19.831
Charlie: So, that's streaky bacon.

00:28:19.831 --> 00:28:21.900
Streaky bacon? So, this is bacon,

00:28:21.900 --> 00:28:25.136
and the other thing was
Canadian bacon in the US.

00:28:25.136 --> 00:28:28.339
I don't know why. Or ham,
I'm going to call it.

00:28:28.339 --> 00:28:30.041
I mean, this just looks like,

00:28:30.041 --> 00:28:31.476
I mean, this looks like whatever.

00:28:34.479 --> 00:28:36.347
Yeah, this sucks. And that's why it sucks.

00:28:36.347 --> 00:28:38.817
It's like, the flatbread is too strong.

00:28:38.817 --> 00:28:40.385
I can barely taste the streaky bacon,

00:28:40.385 --> 00:28:41.953
which is what I came here for, so.

00:28:41.953 --> 00:28:44.522
Double sausage. OK, so with this,

00:28:44.522 --> 00:28:46.491
you guys just went double meat on both.

00:28:48.993 --> 00:28:51.396
Oh, man! Yo!

00:28:51.396 --> 00:28:54.899
Look how much sausage is
in here. Look at that!

00:28:54.899 --> 00:28:59.404
Hell yeah. Now we're talking, UK. See?

00:28:59.404 --> 00:29:01.172
Although, nothing in between

00:29:01.172 --> 00:29:02.941
the two sausage patties is, like,

00:29:04.109 --> 00:29:05.910
it's gotta go cheese, meat, cheese, meat.

00:29:05.910 --> 00:29:08.947
You can't just do meat. This doesn't work.

00:29:08.947 --> 00:29:11.716
And possibly a sauce. No
sauce is weird for this one.

00:29:11.716 --> 00:29:13.418
Your sausage is weird.

00:29:13.418 --> 00:29:15.987
I would say ours is spicier. Not heat,

00:29:15.987 --> 00:29:18.757
but the flavor of the
sausage is more pronounced

00:29:18.757 --> 00:29:20.191
in the US one compared to this.

00:29:20.191 --> 00:29:22.560
So, I know in the US, our
sausage is made up of,

00:29:23.661 --> 00:29:26.464
and from what I understand,
the UK sausage is made up of.

00:29:27.999 --> 00:29:30.368
And that was all done in post.
I have no idea what it says.

00:29:30.368 --> 00:29:31.936
Like, here's the thing.

00:29:31.936 --> 00:29:34.773
I like the double, but needs more cheese,

00:29:34.773 --> 00:29:36.708
needs to be drowning
in some sort of sauce.

00:29:36.708 --> 00:29:40.245
But this one I'm assuming
then is double bacon.

00:29:42.714 --> 00:29:44.315
No, this is not double bacon.

00:29:44.315 --> 00:29:48.853
Wait, one, two pieces
of bacon's double bacon?

00:29:48.853 --> 00:29:51.556
This is double for you guys? For real?

00:29:51.556 --> 00:29:53.558
Yo, you're getting ripped off, guys.

00:29:53.558 --> 00:29:55.293
Excuse me, you've made a mistake.

00:29:55.293 --> 00:29:57.962
You come back in like, come
storming in and cut in the line,

00:29:57.962 --> 00:29:59.430
be like, "Ah, you made a mistake on mine.

00:29:59.430 --> 00:30:01.166
There's only one slice of bacon on this."

00:30:01.166 --> 00:30:03.968
So, all right. Let's try
with this double bacon.

00:30:05.069 --> 00:30:06.471
I mean, it's ham.

00:30:08.673 --> 00:30:12.477
Yeah, that's standard. That's not double.

00:30:12.477 --> 00:30:13.645
This is smart that they did the jam.

00:30:13.645 --> 00:30:16.681
I don't know in the US they
have the squirtable one.

00:30:16.681 --> 00:30:17.816
I mean, do I need to, like,

00:30:17.816 --> 00:30:20.118
I mean, I know what a
muffin and jam taste like.

00:30:20.118 --> 00:30:21.186
I'm not like ...

00:30:21.186 --> 00:30:23.855
Harry: Have you had a
British muffin and jam?

00:30:23.855 --> 00:30:24.689
If I eat this,

00:30:24.689 --> 00:30:27.659
will I still have had a
British muffin and jam?

00:30:27.659 --> 00:30:29.360
I think after this, I
still will have no idea

00:30:29.360 --> 00:30:31.196
what a British muffin and jam taste like.

00:30:31.196 --> 00:30:31.996
All right, all right, all right.

00:30:31.996 --> 00:30:33.498
All right, everyone relax.

00:30:35.867 --> 00:30:37.569
Oh, yeah, that is really good.

00:30:37.569 --> 00:30:39.571
This tastes way better
than the crap that we have.

00:30:39.571 --> 00:30:40.738
Like, way better!

00:30:40.738 --> 00:30:42.440
So, I have just been
informed that in England,

00:30:42.440 --> 00:30:44.642
these are just called
muffins, not English muffins.

00:30:44.642 --> 00:30:48.146
Porridge. I'm from the US.

00:30:48.146 --> 00:30:51.216
I don't know what porridge
is. I'm assuming it's oatmeal?

00:30:51.216 --> 00:30:53.051
So, from what I can tell,

00:30:53.051 --> 00:30:54.452
you can get porridge four different ways.

00:30:54.452 --> 00:30:56.888
One with golden syrup,
looks a lot like honey;

00:30:56.888 --> 00:31:00.091
one with strawberry jam,
straight from France;

00:31:00.091 --> 00:31:03.027
one with sugar, which
they did not include;

00:31:03.027 --> 00:31:04.362
and then one plain.

00:31:04.362 --> 00:31:08.700
So, first I'm just going
straight porridge, no chaser.

00:31:08.700 --> 00:31:11.002
Yeah, that has no flavor to it.

00:31:11.002 --> 00:31:12.203
Leon: Have some golden syrup on the side.

00:31:12.203 --> 00:31:13.571
Yeah, all right.

00:31:13.571 --> 00:31:16.741
So, I've been informed that
golden syrup is good stuff.

00:31:16.741 --> 00:31:18.409
I don't know what's the
difference between golden syrup

00:31:18.409 --> 00:31:21.346
and I guess whatever other syrups.

00:31:21.346 --> 00:31:22.247
You're right, it's like,

00:31:22.247 --> 00:31:25.850
it's not quite maple syrup,
but it's pretty close.

00:31:25.850 --> 00:31:27.318
Makes it much better, obviously.

00:31:29.821 --> 00:31:32.457
Joe: All right. Overall, Harry,
of the American exclusives,

00:31:32.457 --> 00:31:35.526
what were some of your likes
and some of your dislikes?

00:31:35.526 --> 00:31:37.462
Hm. Some of the things I liked,

00:31:37.462 --> 00:31:40.198
you guys have a much bigger
breakfast menu than we do.

00:31:40.198 --> 00:31:41.199
I did like the McGriddles.

00:31:41.199 --> 00:31:43.401
They did live up to Joe's
pretty high billing.

00:31:43.401 --> 00:31:44.235
Joe: Mm-hmm.

00:31:44.235 --> 00:31:46.871
I also think that your bacon
is much better than ours.

00:31:46.871 --> 00:31:49.340
So I think maybe the double
Quarter Pounder with bacon

00:31:49.340 --> 00:31:51.509
was a strong highlight there.

00:31:51.509 --> 00:31:54.412
Some dislikes, there's a few.

00:31:54.412 --> 00:31:56.814
I don't like the
biscuits. I'm sorry, guys.

00:31:56.814 --> 00:31:58.249
I think they are, like,

00:31:58.249 --> 00:32:00.285
for a British person,
too similar to a scone.

00:32:00.285 --> 00:32:02.020
So we can't really mentally differentiate

00:32:02.020 --> 00:32:04.989
between the two, and it's just quite dry.

00:32:04.989 --> 00:32:07.992
And also I think, like,
making your burgers deluxe

00:32:07.992 --> 00:32:10.528
by just adding loads of mayo, some tomato,

00:32:10.528 --> 00:32:12.664
and lettuce just is a bit underwhelming.

00:32:12.664 --> 00:32:14.232
Not really a deluxe vibe for me.

00:32:14.232 --> 00:32:16.634
Joe: So, if you could
bring one thing to the UK

00:32:16.634 --> 00:32:19.270
from the US, exclusive, what would it be?

00:32:19.270 --> 00:32:20.705
If I could take one of these exclusives

00:32:20.705 --> 00:32:23.374
that I've tried today back to
the UK with me for our menu,

00:32:23.374 --> 00:32:24.242
I think I'm going to have to pick

00:32:24.242 --> 00:32:25.777
the bacon, egg, and cheese McGriddle.

00:32:25.777 --> 00:32:26.844
I think it was really good.

00:32:26.844 --> 00:32:29.547
It's a bit of a twist on the
classic McMuffin formula.

00:32:29.547 --> 00:32:31.282
Feels a little bit more decadent, maybe,

00:32:31.282 --> 00:32:32.951
a little bit more sweet.

00:32:32.951 --> 00:32:34.552
And, yeah, just really good fun.

00:32:34.552 --> 00:32:36.721
I like the emphasis you guys
place on your breakfast menu.

00:32:36.721 --> 00:32:37.922
Joe: And what was the thing
you just hated the most,

00:32:37.922 --> 00:32:39.791
you're like, "Ugh, let
that stay in the US"?

00:32:40.792 --> 00:32:42.694
Well, the thing that I hated the most

00:32:42.694 --> 00:32:46.397
and would want to remove
from all possible menus,

00:32:46.397 --> 00:32:48.633
it's tricky. There are a couple.

00:32:49.867 --> 00:32:52.036
But I think it might have
to be the sausage biscuit.

00:32:52.036 --> 00:32:53.705
It was so dry.

00:32:53.705 --> 00:32:57.809
And the notion of a
biscuit-slash-scone breakfast sandwich

00:32:57.809 --> 00:32:59.811
to a British person is just too bizarre.

00:32:59.811 --> 00:33:03.114
I can't get my head around
it. And, yeah, not the best.

00:33:03.114 --> 00:33:04.716
Gotta say, I really disliked your bacon.

00:33:04.716 --> 00:33:06.451
Your bacon is weird.

00:33:06.451 --> 00:33:08.252
It ruined everything that it was on.

00:33:08.252 --> 00:33:11.756
I love bacon, but your bacon
is just, it is bizarre.

00:33:11.756 --> 00:33:13.324
The things I liked the most,

00:33:13.324 --> 00:33:15.360
I obviously like the curry dipping sauce.

00:33:15.360 --> 00:33:18.062
I like the banana milkshake,
separately, obviously.

00:33:18.062 --> 00:33:20.732
That triple chocolate
chip cookie was good.

00:33:20.732 --> 00:33:21.933
Harry: All right, Joe,
you gotta pick one thing

00:33:21.933 --> 00:33:23.735
to take back with you
to the US from our menu

00:33:23.735 --> 00:33:25.236
and you gotta pick one thing to remove

00:33:25.236 --> 00:33:26.771
from our menu forever.

00:33:26.771 --> 00:33:30.141
I'm taking back the curry dipping sauce.

00:33:30.141 --> 00:33:34.245
I've wanted to try that since
we shot the first episode.

00:33:36.080 --> 00:33:39.050
And then, take off your menu,

00:33:40.118 --> 00:33:42.320
I mean, those veggie
dippers were pretty dismal,

00:33:42.320 --> 00:33:46.290
but I don't want to leave
vegetarians out in the lurch.

00:33:46.290 --> 00:33:48.793
The thing that's, like,
haunting me the most

00:33:48.793 --> 00:33:51.429
was the grilled-chicken wrap.

00:33:51.429 --> 00:33:53.464
I don't even think it was
grilled. I think it was boiled.

00:33:53.464 --> 00:33:57.368
And I feel bad that that's
on your menu, and it's gross.

00:33:57.368 --> 00:34:00.805
And I will do the UK a favor:

00:34:00.805 --> 00:34:02.740
all grilled chicken off
the menu, McDonald's.

00:34:02.740 --> 00:34:03.574
You're welcome.

00:34:04.008 --> 00:34:05.910
Joe: A Brit and an American swap countries

00:34:05.910 --> 00:34:09.947
to try each other's KFC.
This is "Food Wars."

00:34:12.850 --> 00:34:14.152
We're going to start with
some things you can get

00:34:14.152 --> 00:34:16.154
in both the US and the UK
to see if there are some

00:34:16.154 --> 00:34:18.322
subtle differences in
taste or anything else.

00:34:18.322 --> 00:34:19.257
The first thing for me to try,

00:34:19.257 --> 00:34:20.792
the main event, the fried chicken.

00:34:20.792 --> 00:34:22.293
So, this is just original recipe chicken.

00:34:22.293 --> 00:34:24.028
I've got what looks to be a thigh piece.

00:34:24.028 --> 00:34:27.365
Visually, I think it probably
looks slightly more appealing

00:34:27.365 --> 00:34:29.867
than British fried chicken
from KFC tends to look.

00:34:34.338 --> 00:34:35.640
I always struggle to identify

00:34:35.640 --> 00:34:37.775
where the bones are in pieces of KFC.

00:34:37.775 --> 00:34:40.478
I don't want to just bite
straight into a bone.

00:34:40.478 --> 00:34:41.746
Mm-hmm.

00:34:41.746 --> 00:34:43.581
OK, yeah, this is good.

00:34:43.581 --> 00:34:45.083
Compared to the UK, I think I definitely

00:34:45.083 --> 00:34:46.317
am getting more flavor.

00:34:46.317 --> 00:34:48.086
I think a fair amount of that
is coming from the breading.

00:34:48.086 --> 00:34:51.122
It's actual seasoning and flavor.

00:34:51.122 --> 00:34:53.491
It's a thick, juicy piece of chicken.

00:34:53.491 --> 00:34:54.926
I don't want to go back to eating regular

00:34:54.926 --> 00:34:56.461
British KFC after this.

00:34:56.461 --> 00:34:58.229
Right, this six-piece bucket.

00:34:58.229 --> 00:34:59.464
This looks like it has more skin

00:34:59.464 --> 00:35:00.932
than what we got in the
restaurant, I will say.

00:35:00.932 --> 00:35:03.267
So already this looks like
it has a better batter to it.

00:35:05.103 --> 00:35:06.270
That is so bland.

00:35:06.270 --> 00:35:08.473
I can taste the flavor.
It's just not as strong,

00:35:08.473 --> 00:35:10.274
and I'm assuming that's the chemicals

00:35:10.274 --> 00:35:12.877
we put in our food to
make it taste like, wah!

00:35:12.877 --> 00:35:14.145
The next thing that we
wanted to compare was

00:35:14.145 --> 00:35:16.180
popcorn chicken, which I
think in the UK is a pretty

00:35:16.180 --> 00:35:18.049
iconic menu item, although weirdly enough

00:35:18.049 --> 00:35:20.551
they've actually cut it from
the menu in the US right now,

00:35:20.551 --> 00:35:21.419
the exception being that

00:35:21.419 --> 00:35:23.321
they will still add it to famous bowls.

00:35:23.321 --> 00:35:24.288
But we'll get to that later.

00:35:24.288 --> 00:35:25.990
So I guess for the time being I will try

00:35:25.990 --> 00:35:28.292
a US chicken nugget and
see how that compares.

00:35:28.292 --> 00:35:31.262
I mean, this just kind of
looks like popcorn chicken.

00:35:32.930 --> 00:35:35.133
Definitely a bit more dry on the palate.

00:35:35.133 --> 00:35:37.902
Again, I don't see why they've
gotten rid of popcorn chicken

00:35:37.902 --> 00:35:39.770
in lieu of these, because
popcorn chicken is

00:35:39.770 --> 00:35:41.272
effectively the same thing.

00:35:41.272 --> 00:35:42.373
That's like a shot!

00:35:42.373 --> 00:35:44.375
[air horn blowing]

00:35:44.375 --> 00:35:45.309
Oh, half in.

00:35:45.309 --> 00:35:46.744
No. I don't taste anything.

00:35:46.744 --> 00:35:49.447
So far I would say that KFC chicken,

00:35:49.447 --> 00:35:51.349
both on the bone and popcorn,

00:35:51.349 --> 00:35:54.852
in the US, the flavor is more pronounced

00:35:54.852 --> 00:35:57.922
and has more of, like,
a savory flavor to it.

00:35:57.922 --> 00:36:00.091
This flavor has training wheels.

00:36:01.159 --> 00:36:02.059
It'll get there someday!

00:36:04.162 --> 00:36:05.429
Firstly, there are some twists

00:36:05.429 --> 00:36:07.832
on the classic fried chicken
which we can't usually find.

00:36:07.832 --> 00:36:11.502
The first variety we have here
is the spicy fried chicken.

00:36:11.502 --> 00:36:13.971
I mean, visually this looks fairly similar

00:36:13.971 --> 00:36:16.340
to just the sort of
standard original recipe.

00:36:16.340 --> 00:36:19.443
Although I will say the
breading looks pretty good.

00:36:19.443 --> 00:36:21.812
You get a lot of these
little flakes of breading,

00:36:21.812 --> 00:36:24.382
which really tend to get
crisp and stay crisp.

00:36:26.083 --> 00:36:27.618
I don't know if there's
enough to call it spicy,

00:36:27.618 --> 00:36:30.087
because I'm not a guy who has
a super-high spice tolerance,

00:36:30.087 --> 00:36:33.457
and for me that's, like, warm,
but not much more than that.

00:36:33.457 --> 00:36:34.792
But it's very pleasant, and I do think

00:36:34.792 --> 00:36:36.594
it's crispier than the original recipe.

00:36:36.594 --> 00:36:38.062
Very juicy, flavorful.

00:36:38.062 --> 00:36:38.996
I think this is really good.

00:36:38.996 --> 00:36:40.831
I think I would be tempted to buy

00:36:40.831 --> 00:36:43.167
this over just classic original recipe.

00:36:43.167 --> 00:36:45.169
And it's not just spicy chicken
that's available in the US.

00:36:45.169 --> 00:36:47.471
You can also get another
type called extra crispy.

00:36:47.471 --> 00:36:49.273
As the name suggests, it's
the regular fried chicken,

00:36:49.273 --> 00:36:50.575
but made extra crispy.

00:36:50.575 --> 00:36:53.611
I think extra crispy
should be the KFC chicken,

00:36:53.611 --> 00:36:56.547
and then the original
should be, like, diet.

00:36:56.547 --> 00:36:58.216
For some reason, the branch
that we went to today

00:36:58.216 --> 00:37:00.051
didn't have it in the form of regular,

00:37:00.051 --> 00:37:01.419
original recipe chicken,

00:37:01.419 --> 00:37:04.021
but they did have it in the
form of a chicken little.

00:37:04.021 --> 00:37:05.690
I'm just going to break off the end bit

00:37:05.690 --> 00:37:07.091
that was untouched by the mayo

00:37:07.091 --> 00:37:08.926
to see if it is actually crispy or not.

00:37:09.994 --> 00:37:11.462
I don't think this is extra crispy.

00:37:11.462 --> 00:37:13.264
Even though they told us it was.

00:37:13.264 --> 00:37:16.267
Maybe their crispinator was
broken today or something.

00:37:17.768 --> 00:37:20.605
KFC US is very good at
cooking chicken on the bone,

00:37:20.605 --> 00:37:22.907
less good when it comes to
cooking chicken off the bone,

00:37:22.907 --> 00:37:24.709
because this is a little
bit dry, a little bit chewy.

00:37:24.709 --> 00:37:28.079
Moving on, the snack wrap.
This one is the flamin' hot.

00:37:30.748 --> 00:37:32.917
Oh, wow. This has got some heat to it!

00:37:32.917 --> 00:37:34.318
OK, UK!

00:37:34.318 --> 00:37:36.454
Yeah, that's, I like
this. This is really good.

00:37:36.454 --> 00:37:38.256
Kansas barbecue. OK.

00:37:39.590 --> 00:37:40.992
This barbecue sauce is pretty good.

00:37:40.992 --> 00:37:42.627
I mean, this is definitely
a sweeter sauce,

00:37:42.627 --> 00:37:45.863
which I think is indicative
of Kansas City barbecue.

00:37:45.863 --> 00:37:46.864
Anyway, yeah, not bad.

00:37:46.864 --> 00:37:48.466
Sweet chili bites.

00:37:50.434 --> 00:37:52.303
Too sweet. Not that spicy.

00:37:52.303 --> 00:37:54.171
Now we're on to an item
which I've been watching from

00:37:54.171 --> 00:37:56.974
across the pond with a mixture
of horror and fascination.

00:37:56.974 --> 00:37:59.176
It's the KFC famous bowl.

00:37:59.176 --> 00:38:00.344
Instead of me trying to explain it,

00:38:00.344 --> 00:38:01.746
I feel like we should
just get Joe in here.

00:38:01.746 --> 00:38:03.714
Joe, do you want to come and
explain the famous bowl to me?

00:38:03.714 --> 00:38:05.116
A little bit of everything
that's on the menu,

00:38:05.116 --> 00:38:06.884
just in bowl form,

00:38:06.884 --> 00:38:09.020
for anyone who just pretty
much has given up on life

00:38:09.020 --> 00:38:11.555
and doesn't care as long as
they get it in the stomach.

00:38:11.555 --> 00:38:12.623
Thanks, Joe.
Joe: You're welcome.

00:38:12.623 --> 00:38:14.692
Harry: It's looking more like
an infamous bowl right now.

00:38:14.692 --> 00:38:15.760
I'm going to ...

00:38:17.928 --> 00:38:19.363
It's not horrible.

00:38:19.363 --> 00:38:20.931
There's just a lot going on.

00:38:20.931 --> 00:38:22.733
There's a lot of flavors fighting

00:38:22.733 --> 00:38:25.503
with each other right
now, vying for supremacy.

00:38:25.503 --> 00:38:28.172
The main thing I get I
think is the corn, actually.

00:38:28.172 --> 00:38:30.141
I would've assumed that
the mash and the chicken

00:38:30.141 --> 00:38:32.176
would've been kind of
the stars of the show.

00:38:32.176 --> 00:38:34.045
But if anything, it's
everything else in there

00:38:34.045 --> 00:38:36.180
that you can actually taste more.

00:38:36.180 --> 00:38:37.615
To me, it feels a little bit

00:38:37.615 --> 00:38:39.984
like you're eating baby food for adults.

00:38:39.984 --> 00:38:41.852
I was going to say I'm more
excited to try the next bowl,

00:38:41.852 --> 00:38:43.521
but I don't know if excited is the word.

00:38:43.521 --> 00:38:45.723
Maybe less anxious to try the next bowl.

00:38:45.723 --> 00:38:48.426
This is the KFC mac 'n' cheese bowl,

00:38:48.426 --> 00:38:52.396
but the kind of color on that
is some cause for concern.

00:38:54.398 --> 00:38:58.002
So, I think this actually works
in harmony with the chicken

00:38:58.002 --> 00:38:59.637
much better than the famous bowl does.

00:38:59.637 --> 00:39:01.906
If I had to get a bowl, I
think I would be leaning more

00:39:01.906 --> 00:39:04.175
towards the mac 'n' cheese
bowl than the famous bowl.

00:39:04.175 --> 00:39:06.344
Next up is the KFC pot pie.

00:39:06.344 --> 00:39:08.979
It's funny to see this on
the menu at a KFC in the US

00:39:08.979 --> 00:39:10.715
because I feel like meat pies

00:39:10.715 --> 00:39:12.883
are generally associated
with Britain more.

00:39:12.883 --> 00:39:14.418
We love a meat pie in the UK.

00:39:14.418 --> 00:39:17.021
Steak pie, chicken pie,

00:39:17.021 --> 00:39:19.390
Greggs, Pukka Pies, all that good stuff.

00:39:19.390 --> 00:39:21.292
So, with a meat pie in the
UK, what you'll often get

00:39:21.292 --> 00:39:22.927
is the pastry on the bottom as well.

00:39:22.927 --> 00:39:24.795
So it's like a self-contained pie.

00:39:24.795 --> 00:39:26.864
Whereas I think with a pot
pie, you just have a layer

00:39:26.864 --> 00:39:28.532
of pastry on top and
then filling underneath,

00:39:28.532 --> 00:39:30.034
and there's no bottom layer of crust.

00:39:30.034 --> 00:39:31.035
But let's find out.

00:39:32.536 --> 00:39:33.904
They haven't skimped on the carrot.

00:39:33.904 --> 00:39:35.272
I taste a lot of the carrot flavor.

00:39:35.272 --> 00:39:38.042
In the UK, for example, with
a meat pie you tend to get

00:39:38.042 --> 00:39:40.711
a gravy that will kind of
run out when you cut into it.

00:39:40.711 --> 00:39:43.280
But this is staying on the spoon.

00:39:43.280 --> 00:39:45.049
It's not running off the spoon.

00:39:45.049 --> 00:39:48.185
It's not great, but it's not bad either.

00:39:48.185 --> 00:39:50.755
It's like, the sauce needs
a little bit more seasoning,

00:39:50.755 --> 00:39:51.956
I think. It's a little bit bland.

00:39:51.956 --> 00:39:53.824
Bit more salt and pepper
would not go amiss there.

00:39:53.824 --> 00:39:55.359
I think with a few minor adjustments,

00:39:55.359 --> 00:39:56.694
they could make this really good,

00:39:56.694 --> 00:39:58.262
and I do think Brits would go for this.

00:39:58.262 --> 00:40:00.231
This is super weird. Look at that!

00:40:00.231 --> 00:40:01.198
There's a hash brown in there.

00:40:01.198 --> 00:40:02.700
What does that have to do with tower?

00:40:02.700 --> 00:40:03.701
Not much.

00:40:06.370 --> 00:40:07.204
Hm.

00:40:07.204 --> 00:40:09.840
I like everything that this is made of.

00:40:09.840 --> 00:40:11.976
Together, I don't think it works.

00:40:11.976 --> 00:40:14.245
If I was to get this, I'd
ask them to separate it

00:40:14.245 --> 00:40:16.180
across three containers

00:40:16.180 --> 00:40:18.783
and just eat the hash
brown, then the chicken,

00:40:18.783 --> 00:40:20.317
finish it off with a slice of cheese.

00:40:20.317 --> 00:40:21.285
There you go.

00:40:21.285 --> 00:40:24.922
This would be closer to
what our extra crispy is.

00:40:24.922 --> 00:40:26.190
So this is supposed to be the spicy one.

00:40:26.190 --> 00:40:27.825
It's going to zing me with spice?

00:40:33.397 --> 00:40:34.231
Not bad.

00:40:34.231 --> 00:40:37.401
It's not that I dislike
anything I've had so far,

00:40:37.401 --> 00:40:42.273
it's that it's all 60%
to 70% as far as flavor

00:40:42.273 --> 00:40:45.443
and intensity that I'm used
to in the United States.

00:40:45.443 --> 00:40:48.112
You can also get yourself a zinger stacker

00:40:48.112 --> 00:40:49.713
and a zinger tower burger.

00:40:49.713 --> 00:40:51.348
Yo, this is a thick one.

00:40:51.348 --> 00:40:52.416
Wow!

00:40:52.416 --> 00:40:55.820
I'm not going to bite into
this, but, man, that's a lot.

00:40:55.820 --> 00:40:58.789
This would be right at
home on the US menu.

00:40:58.789 --> 00:41:00.591
This would be like, "Yes, of course."

00:41:00.591 --> 00:41:01.892
It'd be, like, the double
zinger, and everyone's like,

00:41:01.892 --> 00:41:04.228
"Yeah, of course it's double."

00:41:04.228 --> 00:41:05.429
OK.

00:41:05.429 --> 00:41:07.264
Vegan burger.

00:41:07.264 --> 00:41:09.300
It kind of looks like chicken.

00:41:09.300 --> 00:41:11.402
The mayo pretty much missed it, right?

00:41:11.402 --> 00:41:12.436
See how it came?

00:41:12.436 --> 00:41:15.039
So I gotta kind of activate the mayo.

00:41:16.740 --> 00:41:18.976
Twist your vegan sandwich
before you eat it!

00:41:18.976 --> 00:41:20.945
Should I even ask what the mayo's made of?

00:41:23.981 --> 00:41:25.216
I mean, when you rip it apart, it's like

00:41:25.216 --> 00:41:27.718
one of those big erasers that
you get when you're a kid.

00:41:27.718 --> 00:41:29.787
I mean, I wouldn't just
want to eat this in general,

00:41:29.787 --> 00:41:33.357
but as far as a fake
meat, it's pretty close.

00:41:33.357 --> 00:41:34.692
And I don't know why if you were vegan

00:41:34.692 --> 00:41:38.128
you'd be like, "Finally, a
chicken sandwich at KFC."

00:41:38.128 --> 00:41:39.497
No, you can eat this, there's
no chicken meat in it.

00:41:39.497 --> 00:41:40.464
It's like, yeah, but you're still

00:41:40.464 --> 00:41:42.132
killing them by the millions.

00:41:42.132 --> 00:41:43.534
So, there is a category in the menu

00:41:43.534 --> 00:41:45.769
of twisters, rice boxes, and salads.

00:41:45.769 --> 00:41:48.272
They had no rice boxes or salads.

00:41:48.272 --> 00:41:51.075
They did, however, have the twisters.

00:41:52.710 --> 00:41:54.245
But this is called a twister, not a wrap.

00:41:54.245 --> 00:41:55.412
Leon: It's twisted.

00:41:55.412 --> 00:41:56.380
What's twisted about it?

00:41:56.380 --> 00:41:57.214
Well, it's not twisted.

00:41:57.214 --> 00:41:59.617
It looks like they took a chicken
breast and cut it in half.

00:41:59.617 --> 00:42:01.752
And this was, like, one long tender.

00:42:02.853 --> 00:42:04.154
I mean, it's also smaller.

00:42:04.154 --> 00:42:07.925
I bet they wanted to appeal
to a more male demographic.

00:42:07.925 --> 00:42:09.827
So, "Don't get a wrap, get a twister!

00:42:09.827 --> 00:42:11.495
I'm a big man! I don't want a wrap.

00:42:11.495 --> 00:42:13.731
I want a twister! Yeah, it's twisted!

00:42:13.731 --> 00:42:14.732
Wraps are for the ladies,

00:42:14.732 --> 00:42:17.334
but the dudes have twisters. Ah!"

00:42:17.334 --> 00:42:18.969
I don't think that, they think that.

00:42:18.969 --> 00:42:20.371
KFC, shame on you.

00:42:20.371 --> 00:42:21.805
Let's talk about some exclusive sides

00:42:21.805 --> 00:42:23.240
that you can't find in the UK.

00:42:23.240 --> 00:42:24.808
Firstly, if the mac 'n' cheese bowl is

00:42:24.808 --> 00:42:26.343
too much mac 'n' cheese for you,

00:42:26.343 --> 00:42:28.445
you can just get a little cup as a side.

00:42:28.445 --> 00:42:30.714
You can also get a side of corn.

00:42:30.714 --> 00:42:32.449
You guys just produce so much of it.

00:42:32.449 --> 00:42:33.984
You can't get rid of it fast enough.

00:42:33.984 --> 00:42:37.254
I'm not trying corn on the cob.

00:42:37.254 --> 00:42:42.192
Here in the UK, you guys
have corn on the cob.

00:42:42.192 --> 00:42:45.296
Obviously ours is corn off the
cob, but this would be easier

00:42:45.296 --> 00:42:47.531
for driving or eating on the go, right?

00:42:47.531 --> 00:42:49.033
Have you ever seen someone
walking down the street

00:42:49.033 --> 00:42:50.935
just chewing on a cob on a stick?

00:42:50.935 --> 00:42:52.236
It's on a stick!

00:42:52.236 --> 00:42:53.337
You've never seen that?

00:42:53.337 --> 00:42:55.573
Keep your eyes peeled. I would
like to get that trend going.

00:42:55.573 --> 00:42:57.007
And, of course, apparently it wouldn't be

00:42:57.007 --> 00:42:59.577
a US fast-food menu without biscuits.

00:42:59.577 --> 00:43:01.245
This is an American biscuit.

00:43:01.245 --> 00:43:02.846
It looks a lot like a British scone,

00:43:02.846 --> 00:43:03.914
at least on the outside.

00:43:03.914 --> 00:43:06.517
However, generally I think
it's a bit more bready

00:43:06.517 --> 00:43:08.852
and maybe slightly drier than a scone.

00:43:08.852 --> 00:43:10.220
[thudding]

00:43:10.220 --> 00:43:11.221
Texture check.

00:43:12.323 --> 00:43:14.124
It's confusing because
with a British scone,

00:43:14.124 --> 00:43:15.960
they're generally sweetened with sugar

00:43:15.960 --> 00:43:17.828
because they're eaten with
things like jam and cream,

00:43:17.828 --> 00:43:20.364
and it's more of an afternoon
tea/dessert type thing,

00:43:20.364 --> 00:43:21.799
whereas these ones are
supposed to be eaten

00:43:21.799 --> 00:43:24.868
with a savory meal but
actually smell kind of sweet.

00:43:24.868 --> 00:43:26.270
I think of the biscuits I've tried

00:43:26.270 --> 00:43:28.639
from fast-food menus in the US so far,

00:43:28.639 --> 00:43:29.873
this is probably my favorite one,

00:43:29.873 --> 00:43:31.075
but it's somewhere between, like,

00:43:31.075 --> 00:43:33.377
a British scone and a bread roll.

00:43:33.377 --> 00:43:34.311
Baked beans.

00:43:35.613 --> 00:43:39.016
Ugh. Eh. Yeah, these
are way more tomatoey.

00:43:39.016 --> 00:43:40.417
To-MAH-to-ey, excuse me.

00:43:40.417 --> 00:43:42.586
The tomato sauce that
it's in is similar to

00:43:42.586 --> 00:43:44.455
whatever Spaghettios come in.

00:43:44.455 --> 00:43:46.056
I will never be in the mood for that.

00:43:46.056 --> 00:43:47.024
Southern rice.

00:43:48.058 --> 00:43:48.926
What the hell?

00:43:48.926 --> 00:43:50.861
I don't know what they think Southern is.

00:43:50.861 --> 00:43:52.496
I'm surprised at how different it is.

00:43:52.496 --> 00:43:54.465
You'd think an international food chain

00:43:54.465 --> 00:43:55.566
would want it to be the same everywhere,

00:43:55.566 --> 00:43:58.068
but playing to the UK tastes, I assume.

00:43:58.068 --> 00:44:00.170
KFC in the US has a bunch of sauce options

00:44:00.170 --> 00:44:02.673
that we can't get in the UK,
which means it's time for:

00:44:02.673 --> 00:44:05.142
Sauce talk, "Foreign Exchange"!

00:44:05.142 --> 00:44:06.910
The theme seems to be that
they have a lot of honey

00:44:06.910 --> 00:44:09.480
on the menu when it comes to
their sauces at KFC in the US.

00:44:09.480 --> 00:44:11.682
The sauces on offer here are hot sauce,

00:44:11.682 --> 00:44:14.485
honey sauce, a honey barbecue sauce,

00:44:14.485 --> 00:44:17.955
KFC sauce, and yet more
honey, a honey mustard.

00:44:17.955 --> 00:44:20.024
I usually like a honey
mustard, but I do think

00:44:20.024 --> 00:44:22.926
you have to get the balance
of honey and mustard right.

00:44:24.328 --> 00:44:25.729
Yeah, that's not bad. That's
a pretty well-balanced

00:44:25.729 --> 00:44:28.565
honey mustard, I think.
I'm intrigued by KFC sauce.

00:44:30.100 --> 00:44:31.101
I quite like it.

00:44:31.101 --> 00:44:32.503
I really can't put my finger on exactly

00:44:32.503 --> 00:44:33.437
what's in it right now.

00:44:33.437 --> 00:44:35.005
Next up we've got the honey barbecue.

00:44:38.008 --> 00:44:39.743
Oh, extremely sweet.

00:44:39.743 --> 00:44:42.212
Both on the honey side and
even on the barbecue side.

00:44:42.212 --> 00:44:43.514
Let's have a look at the honey sauce.

00:44:43.514 --> 00:44:45.683
It's fine. It does taste
pretty much just like honey.

00:44:45.683 --> 00:44:47.618
And then finally they have a hot sauce.

00:44:47.618 --> 00:44:49.653
Yeah, that's pretty comparable
to, like, a Frank's RedHot.

00:44:49.653 --> 00:44:50.754
Barbecue!

00:44:51.989 --> 00:44:53.257
OK, Kentucky smoked barbecue.

00:44:53.257 --> 00:44:54.458
Actually, this is on point.

00:44:54.458 --> 00:44:56.660
Sticky sweet chili sauce.

00:44:56.660 --> 00:44:57.861
Why is it sticky?

00:44:58.762 --> 00:45:00.431
Yeah! Oh, that's good.

00:45:00.431 --> 00:45:02.433
All right, garlic buttermilk mayo.

00:45:02.433 --> 00:45:04.535
I like all three of
those things separately.

00:45:05.936 --> 00:45:07.604
Mm! Yeah, that's pretty good.

00:45:07.604 --> 00:45:09.173
Now let's look at some exclusive drinks

00:45:09.173 --> 00:45:12.209
served in these delightful
"Diablo"-branded cups.

00:45:12.209 --> 00:45:14.912
You guys love a advertisement
tie-in, don't you?

00:45:14.912 --> 00:45:18.382
So, I believe this one is Starry,
Joe's beloved Sierra Mist,

00:45:18.382 --> 00:45:21.819
unfortunately culled recently
and replaced by Starry.

00:45:21.819 --> 00:45:23.554
Let's give it a try.

00:45:23.554 --> 00:45:25.022
It's more what I'm used to, I guess,

00:45:25.022 --> 00:45:28.158
from a UK version of a
lemonade-style drink.

00:45:28.158 --> 00:45:31.195
And, of course, we have
a US-style lemonade.

00:45:32.696 --> 00:45:34.998
It's pretty good. Again,
to me it's slightly weird

00:45:34.998 --> 00:45:36.500
what Americans consider lemonade,

00:45:36.500 --> 00:45:38.102
considering coming from the UK,

00:45:38.102 --> 00:45:39.603
lemonade is basically Sprite.

00:45:39.603 --> 00:45:42.139
It's a clear, carbonated, lemony beverage.

00:45:42.139 --> 00:45:42.973
It's pretty good.

00:45:42.973 --> 00:45:45.709
It's probably slightly more
refreshing and hydrating

00:45:45.709 --> 00:45:47.311
than a Sprite is in the UK.

00:45:47.311 --> 00:45:48.746
There are a couple of
other exclusive drinks

00:45:48.746 --> 00:45:49.613
which we can normally get,

00:45:49.613 --> 00:45:51.815
but unfortunately our
local branch did not have,

00:45:51.815 --> 00:45:53.517
devastatingly, because I really wanted

00:45:53.517 --> 00:45:55.919
to try the Mountain Dew Sweet Lightning

00:45:55.919 --> 00:45:57.788
and regular American Mountain Dew.

00:45:57.788 --> 00:45:59.823
When we ordered the bottles
of drinks, didn't we think

00:45:59.823 --> 00:46:02.726
it was just going to be, like,
a personal one? I don't know.

00:46:02.726 --> 00:46:04.428
Tango, orange.

00:46:04.428 --> 00:46:06.029
Ugh, 7Up free.

00:46:06.029 --> 00:46:07.264
Pepsi Max cherry.

00:46:07.264 --> 00:46:09.933
Krushems! UK of course has
exclusive Krushem drinks.

00:46:09.933 --> 00:46:11.635
I have them in front of me. I
said, "Give me one of each,"

00:46:11.635 --> 00:46:14.071
and they did. Milkybar.

00:46:14.071 --> 00:46:14.905
Mm!

00:46:14.905 --> 00:46:16.373
Aero. Is that normal?

00:46:16.373 --> 00:46:19.610
Charlie: It kind of was advertised
as a "healthy" chocolate.

00:46:19.610 --> 00:46:22.846
Leon: Because it's got more
air in there. It's healthy.

00:46:22.846 --> 00:46:24.081
We're still charging the same,

00:46:24.081 --> 00:46:26.350
but you get less in there, so, OK.

00:46:26.350 --> 00:46:29.286
Less calories by default
because it's filled with air.

00:46:29.286 --> 00:46:30.754
I might be the last
person to point this out,

00:46:30.754 --> 00:46:31.822
but, like, they took the candy bar,

00:46:31.822 --> 00:46:34.625
and they crushed it, and
that's why it's Krushems. OK.

00:46:34.625 --> 00:46:36.693
Oreo one. I mean, come on.

00:46:36.693 --> 00:46:38.862
That's really good. I
would definitely get this.

00:46:38.862 --> 00:46:39.696
Dessert.

00:46:39.696 --> 00:46:42.166
Exclusive desserts. You get a
white chocolate chip cookie.

00:46:42.166 --> 00:46:44.067
You can also get a pineapple stick,

00:46:44.067 --> 00:46:45.969
but they didn't have any
at the location we went to.

00:46:45.969 --> 00:46:48.739
Also, I don't know what
a pineapple stick is.

00:46:48.739 --> 00:46:50.774
Leon: It's a terrible dessert.
Joe: Why is that dessert?

00:46:53.110 --> 00:46:55.212
I think if I could pick
one item from this menu

00:46:55.212 --> 00:46:57.181
to take back with me to the UK

00:46:57.181 --> 00:46:58.382
and put on our menu over there,

00:46:58.382 --> 00:47:00.384
I think it would probably
be the spicy chicken.

00:47:00.384 --> 00:47:01.985
I just like how it was
slightly more crispy

00:47:01.985 --> 00:47:04.321
than the regular chicken and
just added a bit more flavor.

00:47:04.321 --> 00:47:05.856
The level of heat was really good.

00:47:05.856 --> 00:47:07.224
Yeah, I think that
would come back with me.

00:47:07.224 --> 00:47:10.227
If I could remove one thing
from the US and all other menus

00:47:10.227 --> 00:47:12.930
from KFC, I think it
would be the famous bowl.

00:47:12.930 --> 00:47:14.331
I'm sorry, guys. I don't want to start

00:47:14.331 --> 00:47:16.233
some kind of revolutionary war again,

00:47:16.233 --> 00:47:18.402
but I just feel like it's not very good,

00:47:18.402 --> 00:47:20.904
because those ingredients
don't really go together,

00:47:20.904 --> 00:47:22.639
texturally, it's a bit of a nightmare,

00:47:22.639 --> 00:47:24.074
and honestly there's
just way better things

00:47:24.074 --> 00:47:25.809
you can do with the stuff on the menu.

00:47:25.809 --> 00:47:29.213
I was really impressed
with the flamin' hot wrap.

00:47:29.213 --> 00:47:30.380
I might have dogged on
it a little bit earlier

00:47:30.380 --> 00:47:32.549
because it was smaller,
but that spicy sauce

00:47:32.549 --> 00:47:34.117
you guys have is actually pretty good.

00:47:34.117 --> 00:47:36.420
Honorable mention, the vegan burger.

00:47:36.420 --> 00:47:40.157
Obviously, I'm not vegan,
but I guess I was surprised

00:47:40.157 --> 00:47:42.693
by how kind of decent it was.

00:47:42.693 --> 00:47:43.861
It's not my favorite, but, I mean,

00:47:43.861 --> 00:47:47.097
points for it being edible. Way to go.

00:47:47.097 --> 00:47:48.632
I will do everyone a favor,

00:47:48.632 --> 00:47:50.934
and I will say I'm not
cutting a menu item.

00:47:50.934 --> 00:47:54.605
Let's get that potato
off of your sandwiches.

00:47:54.605 --> 00:47:56.540
They just don't work together, period.

00:47:56.907 --> 00:47:58.709
Joe: A Brit and an American swap countries

00:47:58.709 --> 00:48:00.711
to try each other's Burger Kings.

00:48:00.711 --> 00:48:02.079
This is "Food Wars."

00:48:04.514 --> 00:48:05.916
So, obviously you can get a Whopper meal

00:48:05.916 --> 00:48:07.417
at a UK and a US Burger King.

00:48:07.417 --> 00:48:08.819
But we did want to get
them in both countries

00:48:08.819 --> 00:48:10.554
and compare the two to
see the differences.

00:48:10.554 --> 00:48:12.356
This here of course is
a standard Whopper meal.

00:48:12.356 --> 00:48:13.957
I believe it was the regular size.

00:48:13.957 --> 00:48:16.860
And this would be a small in the US.

00:48:16.860 --> 00:48:18.128
Just a quick visual check,

00:48:18.128 --> 00:48:20.430
I mean, the Whopper itself looks identical

00:48:20.430 --> 00:48:22.332
to the Whopper that I'm
used to seeing in the UK.

00:48:22.332 --> 00:48:23.634
Really, really no changes there.

00:48:23.634 --> 00:48:25.502
The toppings seem to be the same.

00:48:25.502 --> 00:48:28.605
You get the mayo, the pickles,
the lettuce, the tomato,

00:48:28.605 --> 00:48:30.674
onions, and of course
the beef on a sesame bun.

00:48:30.674 --> 00:48:32.542
So that's, yeah, exactly what I'm used to.

00:48:32.542 --> 00:48:35.846
Let's take a look at a UK Whopper.

00:48:36.947 --> 00:48:40.517
Looks exactly the same, so that's good.

00:48:41.652 --> 00:48:44.221
Same size. Yeah, it's a big one, right?

00:48:44.221 --> 00:48:45.956
Same stuff on the inside.

00:48:45.956 --> 00:48:47.324
Oh, and I got a regular one.

00:48:47.324 --> 00:48:50.060
I didn't even get it with
cheese, which is rare for me.

00:48:51.762 --> 00:48:53.263
That tastes pretty similar
to what I'm used to.

00:48:53.263 --> 00:48:56.099
The beef is pretty
similar, if not identical.

00:48:56.099 --> 00:48:58.135
You still get that flame-grilled thing

00:48:58.135 --> 00:49:00.203
that Burger King is kind of known for.

00:49:00.203 --> 00:49:03.240
American mayo so far has
just been very creamy,

00:49:03.240 --> 00:49:04.841
but pretty much everything
else is the same.

00:49:04.841 --> 00:49:06.610
Overall, very similar to the
Whopper that I'm used to.

00:49:08.078 --> 00:49:11.615
Exactly the same, which is
good. But the fries, however,

00:49:11.615 --> 00:49:13.083
your fries are a bit different, I think.

00:49:13.083 --> 00:49:16.186
Honestly, the fries, this
is a large Whopper meal.

00:49:16.186 --> 00:49:19.022
I was kind of expecting
bigger for the US, you know?

00:49:19.022 --> 00:49:21.391
There's a good portion of
fries, don't get me wrong.

00:49:21.391 --> 00:49:23.527
But I feel like in the US,
if you order a large fries,

00:49:23.527 --> 00:49:25.329
I was expecting, like, a lot of fries.

00:49:25.329 --> 00:49:27.364
They look pretty similar to
the fries that I'm used to.

00:49:27.364 --> 00:49:28.632
They're fairly thick-cut,

00:49:28.632 --> 00:49:30.701
thicker-cut than, like, a McDonald's, so.

00:49:32.703 --> 00:49:35.038
These are pretty good
fries, I have to say.

00:49:35.038 --> 00:49:37.174
I feel like when I go to
a Burger King in the UK,

00:49:37.174 --> 00:49:38.608
I'm not really there for the fries.

00:49:38.608 --> 00:49:41.278
The fries are just very much
a sort of add-on to the meal.

00:49:41.278 --> 00:49:43.046
These are good. These taste way better

00:49:43.046 --> 00:49:44.448
than the fries that I'm
used to from Burger King.

00:49:44.448 --> 00:49:45.682
I don't know what
they've done differently.

00:49:45.682 --> 00:49:47.784
They're quite aggressively salted,

00:49:47.784 --> 00:49:49.152
which I personally really like.

00:49:49.152 --> 00:49:50.454
But they're just well cooked.

00:49:50.454 --> 00:49:52.923
There's a little bit of
crisp on the outside.

00:49:52.923 --> 00:49:55.158
Still quite nice and fluffy on the inside.

00:49:55.158 --> 00:49:57.828
The US Burger King has —
the fries are weird.

00:49:57.828 --> 00:50:01.698
There's some sort of batter to them.

00:50:01.698 --> 00:50:04.334
I can't describe it. They
changed it years ago,

00:50:04.334 --> 00:50:07.004
and they're a more distinct flavor.

00:50:07.004 --> 00:50:08.739
I don't dislike them,
but they're not that great.

00:50:08.739 --> 00:50:11.008
These regular fries, I think I prefer

00:50:11.008 --> 00:50:13.744
the UK Burger King fries
over the US ones, definitely.

00:50:13.744 --> 00:50:15.278
And of course, the fountain Coke.

00:50:15.278 --> 00:50:17.080
I hope that the camera can capture

00:50:17.080 --> 00:50:19.349
the scale of just how large this drink is.

00:50:19.349 --> 00:50:21.118
I have a big head.

00:50:23.587 --> 00:50:26.123
Yeah, I mean, it's
fountain Coke. It's fine.

00:50:26.123 --> 00:50:27.858
Yeah, this regular drink is so tiny.

00:50:27.858 --> 00:50:29.159
I've just been informed that a whopper

00:50:29.159 --> 00:50:31.895
can be considered an insult
in the UK. What does it mean?

00:50:34.931 --> 00:50:36.500
That's funny.

00:50:36.500 --> 00:50:39.036
Have you been called a whopper before?

00:50:39.036 --> 00:50:40.070
Someone called you a whopper?

00:50:44.074 --> 00:50:46.910
I think generally
speaking, fairly familiar.

00:50:46.910 --> 00:50:49.146
Pretty much what I'm used
to in terms of the burger.

00:50:49.146 --> 00:50:50.113
I've enjoyed these fries

00:50:50.113 --> 00:50:51.948
more than I enjoy the British fries.

00:50:51.948 --> 00:50:53.984
And the Coke is too big.

00:50:53.984 --> 00:50:55.819
Dial that back a little
bit, guys. Calm down.

00:50:58.488 --> 00:51:00.891
Here's everything you
can get at a BK in the US

00:51:00.891 --> 00:51:02.292
that you can't find in the UK.

00:51:02.292 --> 00:51:05.262
Here are all the UK Burger King menu items

00:51:05.262 --> 00:51:07.197
I cannot get in the US.

00:51:07.197 --> 00:51:09.299
Let's take a look at
the US beef exclusives.

00:51:09.299 --> 00:51:12.169
We'll start with this, the Whopper Jr.

00:51:12.169 --> 00:51:14.204
Look at this thing. It's tiny!

00:51:14.204 --> 00:51:16.239
I mean, yeah, I think it's
just a scaled-down version

00:51:16.239 --> 00:51:18.175
of the Whopper. It's got all
the same toppings on there.

00:51:18.175 --> 00:51:19.543
Now we're going from one end of the scale

00:51:19.543 --> 00:51:20.477
straight to the other.

00:51:20.477 --> 00:51:23.847
We're going from the junior
Whopper to the triple Whopper.

00:51:23.847 --> 00:51:26.249
As the name suggests, it is a Whopper,

00:51:26.249 --> 00:51:29.019
but instead of the one
patty, you get three.

00:51:29.019 --> 00:51:31.588
I mean, I don't necessarily object

00:51:31.588 --> 00:51:33.723
to the existence of a triple Whopper.

00:51:33.723 --> 00:51:36.226
I will say I've got some
notes on the assembly,

00:51:36.226 --> 00:51:38.195
because there's no layering going on.

00:51:38.195 --> 00:51:39.796
Obviously a Whopper doesn't have cheese.

00:51:39.796 --> 00:51:42.099
This is literally just the toppings

00:51:42.099 --> 00:51:45.469
and then just three meat
patties back to back.

00:51:45.469 --> 00:51:47.070
So I feel like when you bite into this,

00:51:47.070 --> 00:51:50.774
you're just going to get a
big mouthful of just beef.

00:51:50.774 --> 00:51:52.375
I mean, I will try it for science.

00:51:52.375 --> 00:51:54.377
I'll take a little bite of the triple.

00:51:56.480 --> 00:51:58.815
Yeah, that's kind of confirmed my fears.

00:51:58.815 --> 00:52:00.117
I'm also covered in mayo.

00:52:00.117 --> 00:52:01.785
Next up, we're off to Texas,

00:52:01.785 --> 00:52:03.787
because this is a Texas Whopper.

00:52:03.787 --> 00:52:05.489
In case you're wondering
what made this Texan,

00:52:05.489 --> 00:52:07.290
it seems like they've just added

00:52:07.290 --> 00:52:10.494
some jalapeños,
bacon, cheese,

00:52:10.494 --> 00:52:11.061
and mustard

00:52:11.061 --> 00:52:12.395
to a standard
Whopper.

00:52:12.395 --> 00:52:14.264
I don't really know
enough about Texas culture

00:52:14.264 --> 00:52:16.133
to know if that makes
something Texan or not.

00:52:16.133 --> 00:52:18.602
I would've expected
maybe some barbecue sauce

00:52:18.602 --> 00:52:19.803
if you call something Texan,

00:52:19.803 --> 00:52:22.105
but they seem to have not
done that. So, we'll see.

00:52:24.608 --> 00:52:26.243
I'm a big mustard fan,

00:52:26.243 --> 00:52:28.078
so I like the inclusion
of mustard on this.

00:52:28.078 --> 00:52:30.547
Yeah, that's not bad. I don't
know if I would order that

00:52:30.547 --> 00:52:31.715
just over a standard Whopper,

00:52:31.715 --> 00:52:33.416
but I think it's better
than a triple Whopper.

00:52:33.416 --> 00:52:35.318
This is the BK double melt,

00:52:35.318 --> 00:52:39.289
with a signature cheesy sauce
instead of a slab of cheese.

00:52:39.289 --> 00:52:42.492
They just drizzled the, excuse
me, melted liquid cheese.

00:52:42.492 --> 00:52:44.794
The melted cheese is kind
of a nice texture to it.

00:52:44.794 --> 00:52:47.364
A slice of cheese would
just as easily suffice.

00:52:47.364 --> 00:52:51.535
Bacon double cheeseburger XL, Charlie.

00:52:51.535 --> 00:52:54.538
Two patties, cheese in the
middle, cheese in between them.

00:52:54.538 --> 00:52:56.806
Very smart, guys. See?
It makes a difference.

00:52:56.806 --> 00:52:57.774
It's bigger than — in America,

00:52:57.774 --> 00:53:00.310
we have the regular bacon
double cheeseburger.

00:53:00.310 --> 00:53:02.612
This one is a little bit bigger.

00:53:02.612 --> 00:53:05.348
Well, it's extra bigger. So there you go.

00:53:06.383 --> 00:53:08.285
Yeah, I like this.

00:53:08.285 --> 00:53:11.254
And I would probably get this
if I went to Burger King.

00:53:11.254 --> 00:53:13.223
I think this would do
really well in America.

00:53:13.223 --> 00:53:15.425
Come on, two big beef patties,

00:53:15.425 --> 00:53:18.295
dripping with cheese
and bacon. And it's big.

00:53:18.295 --> 00:53:20.997
It's like, its selling
point is that it's big.

00:53:20.997 --> 00:53:22.799
Dude, this would clean up in the US.

00:53:22.799 --> 00:53:24.634
If this is in the US,
we gotta get US bacon.

00:53:24.634 --> 00:53:27.504
Look at this. Come on, guys, look at this.

00:53:27.504 --> 00:53:29.839
How, like, not pink this is.

00:53:29.839 --> 00:53:31.841
This is like, oh, this bacon's bad.

00:53:31.841 --> 00:53:33.210
Then we have two more burger exclusives,

00:53:33.210 --> 00:53:36.880
which are the kings.

00:53:36.880 --> 00:53:39.783
First up, we have the
Single Quarter Pound King.

00:53:39.783 --> 00:53:42.118
This is a single quarter-pound patty

00:53:42.118 --> 00:53:46.189
with some onions, pickles,
cheese, mustard, and ketchup.

00:53:46.189 --> 00:53:47.591
This looks pretty good
to me. This looks like

00:53:47.591 --> 00:53:49.993
a very classic hamburger,
which I'm kind of here for.

00:53:49.993 --> 00:53:51.528
I will say, in general,
what I'm really enjoying

00:53:51.528 --> 00:53:53.230
about all of these burgers is the pickles.

00:53:53.230 --> 00:53:56.066
I feel like America does
pickles way better than we do.

00:53:56.066 --> 00:53:57.601
I thought that was going
to be better than it was.

00:53:57.601 --> 00:53:59.202
I don't know why. I don't
know what's wrong with it.

00:53:59.202 --> 00:54:00.770
There's quite a lot of onion in it.

00:54:00.770 --> 00:54:02.839
Just a lot of raw white onion.

00:54:02.839 --> 00:54:03.673
And then the next one

00:54:03.673 --> 00:54:05.208
I think we might have
had recently on the menu,

00:54:05.208 --> 00:54:06.710
or it might still be
on the menu in the UK,

00:54:06.710 --> 00:54:08.612
but is a bacon king.

00:54:08.612 --> 00:54:10.280
Either way, I thought this
would be a good opportunity

00:54:10.280 --> 00:54:11.948
to talk about fast-food bacon.

00:54:11.948 --> 00:54:13.149
This is a double burger,

00:54:13.149 --> 00:54:14.985
some cheese in the middle and on top,

00:54:14.985 --> 00:54:19.956
along with a few rashers of
bacon, some ketchup, and mayo.

00:54:19.956 --> 00:54:23.860
Let me just prize a bit of
this bacon off this burger

00:54:23.860 --> 00:54:25.495
so we can get a closer look.

00:54:25.495 --> 00:54:29.499
So, this is the famous
American fast-food bacon.

00:54:29.499 --> 00:54:32.168
So, I feel like the US and
the UK do fast-food bacon,

00:54:32.168 --> 00:54:34.704
and I guess bacon in
general, pretty differently.

00:54:34.704 --> 00:54:37.841
This in the UK would be
called a streaky bacon rasher,

00:54:37.841 --> 00:54:39.643
which is where you get
the kind of thin strips,

00:54:39.643 --> 00:54:42.012
as opposed to back bacon,
where you have a medallion

00:54:42.012 --> 00:54:43.546
and then some strip coming off it.

00:54:43.546 --> 00:54:45.448
Generally speaking, in
the UK, fast-food bacon

00:54:45.448 --> 00:54:48.985
tends to be quite a pallid
pink, fairly unappealing color,

00:54:48.985 --> 00:54:50.353
and can be quite floppy as well.

00:54:50.353 --> 00:54:52.122
They don't tend to cook it
basically for long enough.

00:54:52.122 --> 00:54:54.624
I will say this bacon has
a lot more color on it

00:54:54.624 --> 00:54:57.360
than I would expect to see
from British fast-food bacon.

00:54:58.862 --> 00:55:00.597
That's pretty good. I think
that's probably better than

00:55:00.597 --> 00:55:03.767
the bacon that I'm used to
from a British fast-food chain.

00:55:03.767 --> 00:55:05.735
So far, all the bacon I've
had, including this one,

00:55:05.735 --> 00:55:07.170
it just tends to have a better texture.

00:55:07.170 --> 00:55:08.405
There's a bit more chew to it.

00:55:08.405 --> 00:55:10.607
It's just been cooked a
little bit longer, I think.

00:55:10.607 --> 00:55:13.009
Also, it lends itself to
giving it a much nicer color.

00:55:13.009 --> 00:55:15.345
And you definitely get more
of a smoky flavor from it

00:55:15.345 --> 00:55:16.813
that you would expect from good bacon,

00:55:16.813 --> 00:55:19.616
which I don't think you tend
to get from UK fast-food bacon.

00:55:19.616 --> 00:55:24.421
Yeah, the gourmet kings.
Let's go! Ooh! Fancy.

00:55:24.421 --> 00:55:27.123
First one, farmhouse,
straight from the farm.

00:55:27.123 --> 00:55:29.959
You got your rocket, aka arugula.

00:55:29.959 --> 00:55:33.096
You got your ... pickled red onions?

00:55:33.096 --> 00:55:34.931
And, like, a smoky cheddar cheese, right?

00:55:34.931 --> 00:55:36.299
This is actually,

00:55:36.299 --> 00:55:37.667
this is pretty impressive
looking, I gotta say.

00:55:39.035 --> 00:55:41.538
Ooh, brioche bun.

00:55:41.538 --> 00:55:42.639
Now here we go.

00:55:43.807 --> 00:55:46.376
The arugula, or rocket, kind of ruins it.

00:55:46.376 --> 00:55:50.747
I like it, but it's such a strong flavor,

00:55:50.747 --> 00:55:55.151
it just really tastes like
arugula, rocket, whatever.

00:55:55.151 --> 00:55:56.720
So having a bite without
it is a lot better.

00:55:56.720 --> 00:55:59.689
So, unfortunately I think
the arugula's a little much.

00:55:59.689 --> 00:56:02.892
This one also has arugula on it, so uh-oh.

00:56:02.892 --> 00:56:03.827
Let's get a look in there, man.

00:56:03.827 --> 00:56:08.031
They got the barbecue
sauce, crispy onions, right?

00:56:08.031 --> 00:56:10.367
And the same cheddar, same fun cheddar.

00:56:10.367 --> 00:56:12.035
The arugula's kind of still
a little overpowering,

00:56:12.035 --> 00:56:13.937
but with the fun stuff, and
this cheese that's on here

00:56:13.937 --> 00:56:16.106
is really good, the smoked cheddar.

00:56:16.106 --> 00:56:18.174
This one's good. I would
get this. I like this.

00:56:18.174 --> 00:56:19.809
So steakhouse over farmhouse.

00:56:19.809 --> 00:56:21.010
Then we have a couple of very adorable

00:56:21.010 --> 00:56:22.746
tiny burgers down at the end.

00:56:22.746 --> 00:56:24.948
This one is the Rodeo burger.

00:56:24.948 --> 00:56:27.384
So we're going back to
the South for this one.

00:56:27.384 --> 00:56:28.985
To make this Rodeo, they've added

00:56:28.985 --> 00:56:31.121
barbecue sauce and some onion rings.

00:56:31.287 --> 00:56:33.156
See, the only reason I
can think of onion rings

00:56:33.156 --> 00:56:34.391
counting as Rodeo is that

00:56:34.391 --> 00:56:36.493
maybe it looks a little bit like a lasso.

00:56:38.261 --> 00:56:39.028
Lasso.

00:56:39.462 --> 00:56:40.029
No.

00:56:40.029 --> 00:56:42.098
And then finally we just
have a double cheeseburger.

00:56:42.098 --> 00:56:44.734
You guys got the Memphis barbecue burgers,

00:56:44.734 --> 00:56:47.303
single and double. Go side by side.

00:56:47.303 --> 00:56:48.805
You know, we, in the US, we got something

00:56:48.805 --> 00:56:51.875
called the Rodeo burger. I
don't think you have that here.

00:56:51.875 --> 00:56:53.777
Where it's onion rings and barbecue sauce,

00:56:53.777 --> 00:56:55.145
and it's surprisingly good.

00:56:55.145 --> 00:56:58.615
But it's, like, the smallest
thing. It's, like, that big.

00:56:58.615 --> 00:57:03.186
But this is a good idea.
This is that, but adult size.

00:57:03.186 --> 00:57:04.587
Yeah!

00:57:04.587 --> 00:57:05.955
I gotta get a bite, but I gotta make sure

00:57:05.955 --> 00:57:08.391
I get an onion ring in it, so.

00:57:08.391 --> 00:57:10.393
This works really well together.

00:57:10.393 --> 00:57:11.828
This all works. The creamy mayo,

00:57:11.828 --> 00:57:13.463
the mayo and the barbecue sauce

00:57:13.463 --> 00:57:16.499
and the onion rings, and the bacon?

00:57:16.499 --> 00:57:18.168
Yeah, dude, this is good!

00:57:18.168 --> 00:57:20.236
Another thing that would
do so well in the US.

00:57:20.236 --> 00:57:21.638
I don't know why we don't have this

00:57:21.638 --> 00:57:23.273
in the States, as you say.

00:57:23.273 --> 00:57:24.574
I will say, they'd have to rename it.

00:57:24.574 --> 00:57:26.976
It'd have to be, like, the Rodeo
burger deluxe or something.

00:57:26.976 --> 00:57:28.745
I don't know what about this is Memphis.

00:57:28.745 --> 00:57:31.014
I mean, the barbecue
sauce, it's a sweet sauce.

00:57:31.014 --> 00:57:34.451
I don't know what makes it
"Memphis-y" specifically.

00:57:34.451 --> 00:57:37.887
And I'm still not clear on
why onion rings equals Rodeo.

00:57:37.887 --> 00:57:40.356
Then we're on to some chicken,
fish, and side options.

00:57:40.356 --> 00:57:42.292
We'll start with these ones,
which are chicken fries.

00:57:42.292 --> 00:57:43.359
Now, I'm pretty sure we can get these

00:57:43.359 --> 00:57:45.328
or have had these in the UK before.

00:57:45.328 --> 00:57:46.796
However, when we were recording this,

00:57:46.796 --> 00:57:48.298
it seems as if the only ones available

00:57:48.298 --> 00:57:50.567
are the Doritos chili heatwave version,

00:57:50.567 --> 00:57:53.102
whereas these are the
old-fashioned classic ones.

00:57:53.102 --> 00:57:54.671
These things are great. I love these.

00:57:55.705 --> 00:57:57.574
I don't want to know how
they form the chicken

00:57:57.574 --> 00:57:59.175
into long strips like this.

00:57:59.175 --> 00:58:01.644
If British people are
familiar with Fridge Raiders,

00:58:01.644 --> 00:58:04.147
the snacks, kind of like a bigger,

00:58:04.147 --> 00:58:05.715
hotter version of those. It's great.

00:58:05.715 --> 00:58:07.584
Next up we have a chicken sandwich option,

00:58:07.584 --> 00:58:09.419
which is the chicken Jr.

00:58:09.419 --> 00:58:11.087
As Joe just pointed out,
they love calling things

00:58:11.087 --> 00:58:14.290
"Jr." at Burger King in the US.

00:58:14.290 --> 00:58:17.227
Personally, I think they
should be called the prince.

00:58:17.227 --> 00:58:20.763
You know? You have the
Burger King as the main one.

00:58:20.763 --> 00:58:22.265
The little one should be a prince, surely.

00:58:22.265 --> 00:58:24.167
Like a chicken duke,

00:58:24.167 --> 00:58:28.037
or archbishop of beef.

00:58:28.037 --> 00:58:29.772
It just looks like a very
simple chicken burger.

00:58:31.908 --> 00:58:32.976
That's pretty good.

00:58:32.976 --> 00:58:35.645
The mayo's quite creamy and quite sweet.

00:58:35.645 --> 00:58:37.814
Chicken royale. Looks
just like the regular

00:58:37.814 --> 00:58:41.084
original chicken sandwich we got at BK.

00:58:41.084 --> 00:58:43.620
Longer, though.

00:58:43.620 --> 00:58:45.054
Ah.

00:58:45.054 --> 00:58:48.591
Oh, wait, but this one
has cheese and bacon.

00:58:48.591 --> 00:58:52.462
Hm. Yeah, this looks kind of upsetting.

00:58:54.130 --> 00:58:55.298
Kind of a bummer.

00:58:55.298 --> 00:58:57.934
OK, crispy chicken Memphis style.

00:58:57.934 --> 00:58:59.502
I do like the Memphis style.

00:58:59.502 --> 00:59:02.705
Onion rings and bacon
and chicken with cheese?

00:59:02.705 --> 00:59:04.707
That's a new combination right?

00:59:04.707 --> 00:59:07.577
Yeah. Yeah to this. Yeah!

00:59:07.577 --> 00:59:09.913
I think because it's fried chicken,

00:59:09.913 --> 00:59:13.249
it adds even more flavor to it,

00:59:13.249 --> 00:59:15.018
with the bacon, cheese, and onion rings.

00:59:15.018 --> 00:59:18.988
It's a bit much, but it actually
works pretty well together.

00:59:18.988 --> 00:59:23.826
I think we gotta Memphis up
some of our BK in the US.

00:59:23.826 --> 00:59:26.195
Or just call it Rodeo-style it up.

00:59:26.195 --> 00:59:28.831
Then we have a fish option, the big fish.

00:59:28.831 --> 00:59:32.201
It's fairly reminiscent of a
Filet-O-Fish from McDonald's,

00:59:32.201 --> 00:59:34.003
in that it's got that kind of shiny bun.

00:59:34.003 --> 00:59:36.439
I do like a good fish sandwich.

00:59:38.174 --> 00:59:39.375
Yeah, that's really not bad.

00:59:39.375 --> 00:59:42.445
The fish is, like, fine.
It doesn't taste of a ton.

00:59:42.445 --> 00:59:44.013
An acceptable attempt at a fish sandwich.

00:59:44.013 --> 00:59:46.149
Probably not quite as
good as a Filet-O-Fish.

00:59:46.149 --> 00:59:48.284
Then we have a side option
we can't find in the UK.

00:59:48.284 --> 00:59:50.353
It's mozzarella sticks.

00:59:50.353 --> 00:59:52.255
I feel like, yeah, we have now hit a point

00:59:52.255 --> 00:59:54.657
where pretty much everywhere
does its own mozzarella stick.

00:59:54.657 --> 00:59:56.726
What I will say is it
comes with a little thing

00:59:56.726 --> 00:59:59.195
of marinara sauce, which
I think is the only

00:59:59.195 --> 01:00:03.666
exclusive sauce at a US Burger King.

01:00:03.666 --> 01:00:06.903
So we can do a very,
very short sauce talk.

01:00:06.903 --> 01:00:07.770
Sauce talk.

01:00:07.770 --> 01:00:09.005
The sauce is pretty strong, actually.

01:00:09.005 --> 01:00:11.774
That's a concentrated tomato flavor.

01:00:11.774 --> 01:00:13.943
It's almost like eating a tomato puree

01:00:13.943 --> 01:00:15.612
rather than a marinara sauce.

01:00:15.612 --> 01:00:17.046
Acceptable mozzarella sticks.

01:00:17.046 --> 01:00:18.715
I probably wouldn't be
rushing toward those again.

01:00:18.715 --> 01:00:19.649
Plant-based Whopper.

01:00:19.649 --> 01:00:21.651
I'm pretty sure I did
this in the US, right?

01:00:21.651 --> 01:00:25.588
But your guys' plant-based
meat is different than ours.

01:00:25.588 --> 01:00:29.592
We have the Impossible meat in the US.

01:00:29.592 --> 01:00:33.963
So, our Impossible
Whopper, Impossible meat

01:00:33.963 --> 01:00:38.034
has a chemical that is under review.

01:00:38.034 --> 01:00:40.503
You guys have a different
plant-based meat than we do.

01:00:40.503 --> 01:00:42.205
So let's see what it tastes like.

01:00:43.039 --> 01:00:45.642
It's not ... bad.

01:00:47.844 --> 01:00:50.680
It's not flame-grilled-flavored enough,

01:00:50.680 --> 01:00:51.547
you know what I mean?

01:00:51.547 --> 01:00:53.549
Like, the Whopper, the
meat, you just taste

01:00:53.549 --> 01:00:56.552
that grill smokiness, charcoaliness,

01:00:56.552 --> 01:00:58.287
whatever you want to call it.

01:00:58.287 --> 01:00:59.889
And this, it looks like
they cooked it the same way,

01:00:59.889 --> 01:01:02.125
but I'm not getting that same
flavor from this meat at all.

01:01:02.125 --> 01:01:03.493
So it still tastes like meat,

01:01:03.493 --> 01:01:04.394
but it doesn't taste like a Whopper.

01:01:04.394 --> 01:01:06.896
It doesn't have that
smoky flavor to it. So.

01:01:06.896 --> 01:01:09.499
And I don't think that has
anything to do with the meat.

01:01:09.499 --> 01:01:12.568
I think you guys have got
to flame grill it more

01:01:12.568 --> 01:01:14.671
or add the same flame-grill
chemicals onto this

01:01:14.671 --> 01:01:15.838
as you do the regular meat.

01:01:15.838 --> 01:01:19.609
This is noticeably different
than the UK Whopper.

01:01:19.609 --> 01:01:21.010
Vegan chicken.

01:01:21.944 --> 01:01:23.846
Ew.

01:01:23.846 --> 01:01:27.150
This looks exactly like the
original chicken sandwich, so.

01:01:29.152 --> 01:01:31.220
There's something weird in here.

01:01:31.220 --> 01:01:32.855
There's something weird to that flavor.

01:01:32.855 --> 01:01:34.257
I'm just going to take a little —

01:01:37.093 --> 01:01:39.195
Oh, this is not a good sign.

01:01:39.195 --> 01:01:40.997
This meat is not easy to pull apart.

01:01:40.997 --> 01:01:42.799
Ah! Ugh.

01:01:44.167 --> 01:01:45.802
Nah, it just tastes weird.

01:01:45.802 --> 01:01:47.503
It doesn't taste like chicken.

01:01:47.503 --> 01:01:49.906
It tastes like it's
flavored like the chicken.

01:01:49.906 --> 01:01:52.775
But the consistency of
it is just different.

01:01:52.775 --> 01:01:54.510
I wouldn't say it was bad.

01:01:54.510 --> 01:01:57.413
It just tastes like it's not chicken.

01:01:57.413 --> 01:01:58.981
These came and went in the US so fast,

01:01:58.981 --> 01:02:00.717
I didn't get a chance to try them.

01:02:00.717 --> 01:02:02.452
But now I finally do.

01:02:02.452 --> 01:02:03.886
Looks like a nugget.

01:02:05.955 --> 01:02:08.124
Yeah, it just tastes like
a fake something or other.

01:02:08.124 --> 01:02:11.427
Maybe the batter on this seems
thicker than regular nuggets,

01:02:11.427 --> 01:02:12.995
so I'm getting almost all batter flavor,

01:02:12.995 --> 01:02:14.230
which I guess isn't that big of a deal.

01:02:14.230 --> 01:02:15.531
This doesn't taste like chicken.

01:02:15.531 --> 01:02:17.800
Again, it's, like, blank.

01:02:17.800 --> 01:02:19.502
It doesn't have much flavor to it.

01:02:19.502 --> 01:02:21.504
Yeah, I mean, I think
you guys gotta step up

01:02:21.504 --> 01:02:24.874
your chemical game, because our
fake meat tastes way better.

01:02:24.874 --> 01:02:25.875
And these are chili cheese bites.

01:02:30.747 --> 01:02:32.815
Actually, not that bad.

01:02:32.815 --> 01:02:34.550
It's mostly — ooh, got a
little bit of heat to them too,

01:02:34.550 --> 01:02:36.486
the jalapeños. Yeah, these are good.

01:02:36.486 --> 01:02:39.288
On to the fries. Cheesy fries.

01:02:39.288 --> 01:02:42.892
Oh, man, this is really phoned in.

01:02:42.892 --> 01:02:45.361
This is really phoned
in. No effort on that.

01:02:45.361 --> 01:02:49.565
Look at the bacon. It's not
crispy. It's, like, right?

01:02:50.633 --> 01:02:54.103
This is the bacon they
have at an omelet station

01:02:54.103 --> 01:02:56.606
to put in your omelet
pre-diced or whatever.

01:02:56.606 --> 01:02:57.774
But this is like, guys,

01:02:57.774 --> 01:03:00.276
it's gotta be crispy or nothing. Come on.

01:03:00.276 --> 01:03:02.411
Nothing to it. It really
seems like a waste.

01:03:02.411 --> 01:03:04.413
All right, sauce-talk time.

01:03:04.413 --> 01:03:06.682
Got the sweet chili
and the smoky barbecue.

01:03:06.682 --> 01:03:08.151
There's also a spicy mayo.

01:03:08.151 --> 01:03:10.319
Wasn't available at the Burger
King we went to. Oh, well.

01:03:10.319 --> 01:03:14.190
It' time for sauce talk,
"Foreign Exchange"!

01:03:14.190 --> 01:03:15.825
Sauce talk.

01:03:15.825 --> 01:03:18.094
The first one, sweet chili, boys.

01:03:18.094 --> 01:03:20.863
Sweet chili is having a moment in the UK.

01:03:22.465 --> 01:03:24.500
It's growing on me. I think
sweet chili's really nice.

01:03:24.500 --> 01:03:26.435
Smoky barbecue.

01:03:26.435 --> 01:03:29.105
Oh, this is a collaboration with

01:03:29.105 --> 01:03:32.008
Bull's-Eye steak sauce, or barbecue sauce.

01:03:32.008 --> 01:03:35.278
Was a big player in the sauce
game a decade or two ago.

01:03:35.278 --> 01:03:37.013
But I feel like I haven't
seen Bull's-Eye in a while.

01:03:37.013 --> 01:03:39.182
Mm, this is pretty good.

01:03:39.182 --> 01:03:40.416
Here are all the US exclusive

01:03:40.416 --> 01:03:42.084
breakfast items from Burger King.

01:03:42.084 --> 01:03:43.920
We'll start on this
end, where we will find

01:03:43.920 --> 01:03:45.655
breakfast biscuit sandwiches.

01:03:45.655 --> 01:03:47.256
Now, if you saw the McDonald's episode,

01:03:47.256 --> 01:03:48.491
you'll know that I didn't really like

01:03:48.491 --> 01:03:50.359
their version of a breakfast biscuit.

01:03:50.359 --> 01:03:51.460
This is the ham, egg, and cheese.

01:03:51.460 --> 01:03:52.862
You can also get a bacon, egg, and cheese

01:03:52.862 --> 01:03:54.330
or a sausage, egg, and cheese.

01:03:54.330 --> 01:03:56.199
Now, I'm still not convinced

01:03:56.199 --> 01:03:57.867
by the notion of a breakfast biscuit.

01:03:57.867 --> 01:04:00.203
To the UK mind, this kind
of looks like a scone.

01:04:00.203 --> 01:04:03.606
I will say this one kind
of feels a bit more buttery

01:04:03.606 --> 01:04:06.242
and a bit more moist than
the McDonald's one did.

01:04:06.242 --> 01:04:07.677
So maybe it won't be as bad.

01:04:10.346 --> 01:04:12.615
It's hard to tell if this is
actually like a scone or not.

01:04:12.615 --> 01:04:15.451
This has more of a sort of bready texture

01:04:15.451 --> 01:04:17.420
than a scone does, for
the British audience.

01:04:17.420 --> 01:04:19.789
I feel like a scone tends
to be a bit more crumbly

01:04:19.789 --> 01:04:22.191
and doughy, whereas
this one is more bready.

01:04:22.191 --> 01:04:23.292
As for the flavor,

01:04:23.292 --> 01:04:25.728
there is a pretty similar
flavor, I would say,

01:04:25.728 --> 01:04:28.397
in that the sort of main
taste you get is butter.

01:04:28.397 --> 01:04:29.432
I don't know. It's pretty good.

01:04:29.432 --> 01:04:31.300
Next up we've got the Croissan'wiches.

01:04:31.300 --> 01:04:33.035
Now, for the uninitiated, like myself,

01:04:33.035 --> 01:04:34.036
this is a breakfast sandwich,

01:04:34.036 --> 01:04:36.272
but instead of a bun or a biscuit,

01:04:36.272 --> 01:04:38.574
they use a cut-in-half croissant.

01:04:38.574 --> 01:04:40.409
These come in the form of
bacon, egg, and cheese;

01:04:40.409 --> 01:04:43.613
a sausage, egg, and cheese;
a ham, egg, and cheese;

01:04:43.613 --> 01:04:45.448
or you can get a fully loaded option,

01:04:45.448 --> 01:04:47.250
which comes with all of the above.

01:04:47.250 --> 01:04:49.352
You get the bacon, you get the ham,

01:04:49.352 --> 01:04:50.987
and you get the sausage patty.

01:04:50.987 --> 01:04:52.255
Coming from a country that is

01:04:52.255 --> 01:04:53.689
in pretty close proximity to France,

01:04:53.689 --> 01:04:55.191
I feel like I do have to speak up

01:04:55.191 --> 01:04:57.927
on behalf of my French friends out there.

01:04:57.927 --> 01:05:00.029
Because, yeah, they just
look a bit sad, really.

01:05:00.029 --> 01:05:02.265
I will say I kind of have more faith

01:05:02.265 --> 01:05:04.367
in this idea than a biscuit.

01:05:04.367 --> 01:05:07.303
Because at least a
croissant will be hopefully

01:05:07.303 --> 01:05:09.405
flaky and buttery pastry

01:05:09.405 --> 01:05:11.240
and not quite as dry as a biscuit will be.

01:05:11.240 --> 01:05:13.109
I will say, there are
some places in the UK

01:05:13.109 --> 01:05:15.711
that will do a ham and cheese croissant.

01:05:15.711 --> 01:05:17.880
But it's usually a full-size

01:05:17.880 --> 01:05:20.116
kind of crescent-shaped croissant,

01:05:20.116 --> 01:05:21.384
which they would just cut in half

01:05:21.384 --> 01:05:24.153
and then add the cheese, a
bit of ham, and then toast it.

01:05:24.153 --> 01:05:25.755
These, I don't know.

01:05:25.755 --> 01:05:27.924
It's the fact that they've
got the small circular ones.

01:05:27.924 --> 01:05:30.760
So they've clearly been
purpose-built to be buns.

01:05:30.760 --> 01:05:32.461
I'm not really sure about that.

01:05:32.461 --> 01:05:33.296
I'll try the big boy.

01:05:33.296 --> 01:05:35.464
I'll try the fully loaded Croissan'wich.

01:05:37.333 --> 01:05:39.802
It's actually not the
worst delivery system,

01:05:39.802 --> 01:05:42.605
because it is quite thin,
it is quite buttery,

01:05:42.605 --> 01:05:43.572
and you do get a little bit

01:05:43.572 --> 01:05:45.441
of the flakiness that you'd expect.

01:05:45.441 --> 01:05:47.310
As much as I kind of
disagree with the concept

01:05:47.310 --> 01:05:49.679
of a Croissan'wich, if you made me choose

01:05:49.679 --> 01:05:51.614
between one of these
or a breakfast biscuit,

01:05:51.614 --> 01:05:52.615
I do think I'm choosing these,

01:05:52.615 --> 01:05:54.984
because it's closer to just a sandwich.

01:05:54.984 --> 01:05:55.851
For all the Croissan'wiches,

01:05:55.851 --> 01:05:57.486
you can also get a double-meat version.

01:05:57.486 --> 01:05:59.055
So you can get double meat of the bacon,

01:05:59.055 --> 01:06:01.023
of the sausage, and of the ham.

01:06:01.023 --> 01:06:03.392
I don't think you can get a
double fully loaded version,

01:06:03.392 --> 01:06:05.294
because that would just be kind of insane.

01:06:05.294 --> 01:06:07.296
Then we have two
breakfast-burrito options.

01:06:07.296 --> 01:06:09.732
We have the Egg-Normous Burrito

01:06:09.732 --> 01:06:12.368
and the breakfast burrito Jr.

01:06:12.368 --> 01:06:14.303
If this is Jr., then is this his dad?

01:06:14.303 --> 01:06:17.106
My favorite thing to do is
just invent fast-food lore.

01:06:17.106 --> 01:06:18.674
I'm not 100% sure what's
in either of these,

01:06:18.674 --> 01:06:19.642
so let's find out.

01:06:20.710 --> 01:06:22.478
Oh, wow. Some sausage.

01:06:22.478 --> 01:06:25.348
[laughs] Oh, God. Oh, no.

01:06:25.348 --> 01:06:28.918
Oh, God. Oh, oh, there's,
like, rice in it.

01:06:28.918 --> 01:06:31.087
I mean, I've really made a mess of this.

01:06:31.087 --> 01:06:31.921
I'm sorry, guys.

01:06:31.921 --> 01:06:36.726
So, I'm seeing what looks
like half a sausage patty,

01:06:36.726 --> 01:06:39.829
some egg, and what I think is rice.

01:06:41.764 --> 01:06:43.165
Give it a quick try.

01:06:45.368 --> 01:06:48.304
That's a reasonably
palatable breakfast burrito.

01:06:48.304 --> 01:06:50.773
And then the big boy, the Egg-Normous.

01:06:50.773 --> 01:06:51.907
All right, what do we got in here?

01:06:51.907 --> 01:06:53.709
Bacon, quite a lot of rice.

01:06:53.709 --> 01:06:55.011
I'm not seeing any sausage in this one.

01:06:55.011 --> 01:06:57.413
I'm pretty sure it's just
egg, bacon, and rice.

01:06:57.413 --> 01:06:58.714
Let's give it a quick try.

01:06:59.882 --> 01:07:02.151
It's OK. So, to me, this
does taste a little bit

01:07:02.151 --> 01:07:04.820
claggy and hard to chew its way through.

01:07:04.820 --> 01:07:07.089
However, I'm told it's supposed
to come with a salsa verde,

01:07:07.089 --> 01:07:08.624
which I think they've
forgotten to give me.

01:07:08.624 --> 01:07:10.860
So, maybe if I had a salsa with it,

01:07:10.860 --> 01:07:13.696
that would ease the
digestion a little bit.

01:07:13.696 --> 01:07:15.965
Also, this is called
the Egg-Normous Burrito,

01:07:15.965 --> 01:07:16.932
but it's really not very,

01:07:16.932 --> 01:07:19.101
like, this is not enormous, guys.

01:07:19.101 --> 01:07:20.903
Come on. If you're going
to call something enormous,

01:07:20.903 --> 01:07:23.105
we're in America, I
want properly enormous.

01:07:23.105 --> 01:07:25.941
And then finally we have
some French toast sticks.

01:07:25.941 --> 01:07:28.477
What is Burger King US's beef with France?

01:07:28.477 --> 01:07:30.613
They're really just going for France here.

01:07:30.613 --> 01:07:34.350
So, I don't think I've ever
had French toast before.

01:07:34.350 --> 01:07:36.152
It's not really a thing in the UK.

01:07:36.152 --> 01:07:39.555
So, in the UK, we have
eggy bread, or egg bread,

01:07:39.555 --> 01:07:41.290
which is whisked-up eggs.

01:07:41.290 --> 01:07:42.525
But it's a savory thing, because we're not

01:07:42.525 --> 01:07:45.061
putting vanilla and
cinnamon and stuff in it.

01:07:45.061 --> 01:07:46.295
Harry: I will have

01:07:46.295 --> 01:07:49.698
basically just egg in bread
that I will fry in a pan

01:07:49.698 --> 01:07:51.834
and then maybe eat with some ketchup.

01:07:51.834 --> 01:07:54.270
I'm being told I have to
try this with the syrup,

01:07:54.270 --> 01:07:55.538
so let's give that a go.

01:07:56.939 --> 01:07:59.875
British person tries French
toast for the first time.

01:08:03.479 --> 01:08:04.480
I mean, it is pretty good.

01:08:04.480 --> 01:08:06.615
Joe: Yeah, of course. It's French toast.

01:08:06.615 --> 01:08:10.186
This is even more egregious than pancakes.

01:08:10.186 --> 01:08:12.154
Because this is like a churro

01:08:12.154 --> 01:08:13.355
that you then dip in syrup.

01:08:13.355 --> 01:08:14.757
Somehow that's for breakfast.

01:08:14.757 --> 01:08:16.625
Not convinced if that is
a breakfast food or not,

01:08:16.625 --> 01:08:17.626
but it's very tasty.

01:08:17.626 --> 01:08:19.528
One last thing to note is
that at a US Burger King,

01:08:19.528 --> 01:08:21.330
you can actually buy
several burger options

01:08:21.330 --> 01:08:22.565
before 10:30 a.m.

01:08:22.565 --> 01:08:24.200
While they're still
serving the breakfast menu,

01:08:24.200 --> 01:08:27.303
they will also make you a
Whopper and I think a bacon king.

01:08:27.303 --> 01:08:29.805
I'm not really sure who wants
a Whopper at, like, 9 a.m.

01:08:29.805 --> 01:08:31.107
There's obviously exclusive

01:08:31.107 --> 01:08:32.775
Burger King breakfast menu items,

01:08:32.775 --> 01:08:34.977
but since the pandemic,
a lot of Burger Kings

01:08:34.977 --> 01:08:36.679
are still working on a reduced menu.

01:08:36.679 --> 01:08:39.115
They're almost nowhere
to be found. We looked.

01:08:39.115 --> 01:08:40.316
Apparently you're only
finding them in, like,

01:08:40.316 --> 01:08:44.120
service-station locations.
So, we looked around.

01:08:44.120 --> 01:08:46.422
Couldn't find a place
that served them. Sorry.

01:08:46.422 --> 01:08:48.858
Here are some drinks that I
can't usually find in the UK.

01:08:48.858 --> 01:08:51.494
We'll start with this one,
which is Hi-C fruit punch.

01:08:51.494 --> 01:08:54.130
That's such a deeply unnatural color.

01:08:55.297 --> 01:08:57.233
Joe: American drinks, baby!

01:08:57.233 --> 01:08:59.368
High-fructose corn syrup, let's go.

01:08:59.368 --> 01:09:01.704
My British palate has not adjusted

01:09:01.704 --> 01:09:03.772
to American soft drinks yet,

01:09:03.772 --> 01:09:05.875
because this thing is aggressively sweet.

01:09:05.875 --> 01:09:07.409
This one's Dr Pepper. I can't remember

01:09:07.409 --> 01:09:09.945
if this is on the UK
Burger King menu or not.

01:09:09.945 --> 01:09:11.614
But, I mean, I like Dr Pepper in the UK.

01:09:11.614 --> 01:09:13.482
Let's see if it's the same in the US.

01:09:13.482 --> 01:09:15.618
OK, yeah, no, that's
actually pretty comparable.

01:09:15.618 --> 01:09:18.254
Burger King in the US also
has some milkshake options.

01:09:18.254 --> 01:09:20.289
This one is the Oreo cookie shake.

01:09:20.289 --> 01:09:22.224
This comes highly endorsed by Joe.

01:09:22.224 --> 01:09:24.160
Did you say this was your
favorite fast-food shake?

01:09:24.160 --> 01:09:26.028
Joe: I would say, yeah,
one of my favorites, yeah.

01:09:26.028 --> 01:09:26.862
One of his favorites.

01:09:26.862 --> 01:09:27.696
Joe: One of the best ones, yeah.

01:09:27.696 --> 01:09:29.131
High praise. Let's give it a try.

01:09:31.734 --> 01:09:33.536
I mean, yeah, that's delicious.

01:09:34.436 --> 01:09:38.240
That is so thick. The straw
almost isn't up to the task.

01:09:38.240 --> 01:09:40.776
Yeah, that really does taste like Oreos,

01:09:40.776 --> 01:09:42.278
like the filling of the Oreo.

01:09:42.278 --> 01:09:43.879
And then if that's not
enough chocolate for you,

01:09:43.879 --> 01:09:46.515
they also have a chocolate
Oreo cookie milkshake.

01:09:46.515 --> 01:09:48.584
I mean, yeah, it's
basically the same as that

01:09:48.584 --> 01:09:50.352
but I think just with chocolate ice cream

01:09:50.352 --> 01:09:52.188
instead of vanilla ice cream as the base.

01:09:52.188 --> 01:09:54.223
Yeah, I don't think you need
to mess with the formula.

01:09:54.223 --> 01:09:56.125
Stick with the classic.
Stick with vanilla.

01:09:56.125 --> 01:09:58.160
OK, for drinks, Burger Kings in the UK

01:09:58.160 --> 01:10:00.196
also have tea and espresso,

01:10:00.196 --> 01:10:01.964
and the one we went to
didn't have hot drinks.

01:10:01.964 --> 01:10:04.166
And they also have various Capri Suns,

01:10:04.166 --> 01:10:07.203
which they did have and we did
order and they forgot them.

01:10:07.203 --> 01:10:08.537
Then we have some Burger King desserts

01:10:08.537 --> 01:10:09.905
that we can't find in the UK.

01:10:09.905 --> 01:10:12.441
We have two options. Firstly,
chocolate chip cookies.

01:10:12.441 --> 01:10:14.510
Seems like these come in an order of two,

01:10:14.510 --> 01:10:17.279
which have cemented themselves together.

01:10:17.279 --> 01:10:20.149
They don't look brilliant. They're quite

01:10:20.149 --> 01:10:21.317
hard on the outside.

01:10:21.317 --> 01:10:22.618
[cookie banging on table]

01:10:22.618 --> 01:10:24.620
Don't know if cookies are
supposed to make that noise.

01:10:25.454 --> 01:10:27.356
Those are quite overbaked.

01:10:27.356 --> 01:10:29.992
Then we have a slice of
Hershey's sundae pie.

01:10:29.992 --> 01:10:31.493
I'm kind of intrigued by this.

01:10:31.493 --> 01:10:33.095
It's come pretty highly recommended to me.

01:10:33.095 --> 01:10:35.064
I like the packaging. This is quite fun.

01:10:35.064 --> 01:10:36.999
Don't bite your nails, kids.

01:10:36.999 --> 01:10:39.535
Makes it very hard to open
Hershey's sundae pies.

01:10:39.535 --> 01:10:41.203
I really don't know what
to expect from this,

01:10:41.203 --> 01:10:42.938
but I guess I'm just
going to get a scoop out

01:10:42.938 --> 01:10:44.406
and see what happens.

01:10:45.574 --> 01:10:47.243
Is it pastry on the bottom?

01:10:49.178 --> 01:10:50.446
I can't really figure out what's going on.

01:10:50.446 --> 01:10:52.548
There's, I think, like, a sort of cakey,

01:10:52.548 --> 01:10:54.350
biscuit base type thing.

01:10:54.350 --> 01:10:57.419
Yeah, that is very rich
but also very tasty.

01:10:59.822 --> 01:11:01.624
If there was one menu
item that I could keep

01:11:01.624 --> 01:11:03.626
and take back with me to the UK,

01:11:03.626 --> 01:11:04.593
I don't actually know if it would be

01:11:04.593 --> 01:11:07.029
a specific menu item, or
maybe more like an ingredient.

01:11:07.029 --> 01:11:09.031
I think I would take the
bacon that you guys have

01:11:09.031 --> 01:11:11.500
at a US Burger King and
take that back to the UK.

01:11:11.500 --> 01:11:12.568
Because I feel like here it actually

01:11:12.568 --> 01:11:15.437
adds something to a burger, in
terms of texture and flavor,

01:11:15.437 --> 01:11:16.939
whereas in the UK it's just kind of there.

01:11:16.939 --> 01:11:18.474
Like, you don't really notice it.

01:11:18.474 --> 01:11:20.075
And if there's one menu
item that I would delete

01:11:20.075 --> 01:11:21.810
from all possible Burger King menus,

01:11:21.810 --> 01:11:23.012
I think it would be that triple Whopper.

01:11:23.012 --> 01:11:25.381
I think it just really was
everything that is wrong

01:11:25.381 --> 01:11:27.249
with American fast food in general.

01:11:27.249 --> 01:11:29.251
It's just kind of excess
for the sake of excess.

01:11:29.251 --> 01:11:30.486
You don't need that much meat.

01:11:30.486 --> 01:11:32.988
You need some kind of
lubrication in there.

01:11:32.988 --> 01:11:36.592
It's just dry, chewy,
horrible. Get rid of it.

01:11:36.592 --> 01:11:37.459
Harry: So, Joe, you've tried

01:11:37.459 --> 01:11:38.894
all of our Burger King menu items.

01:11:38.894 --> 01:11:40.763
Which one are you taking
back with you to the US?

01:11:40.763 --> 01:11:45.734
I think I like the Memphis
barbecue burgers the best,

01:11:45.734 --> 01:11:47.536
because it was like a Rodeo burger

01:11:47.536 --> 01:11:49.738
but it's bigger and it
had more stuff on it.

01:11:49.738 --> 01:11:51.473
So I think I could really get into that.

01:11:51.473 --> 01:11:54.243
Harry: Then you can knock one
thing off the UK menu forever.

01:11:54.243 --> 01:11:55.077
What's going?

01:11:55.077 --> 01:11:57.279
What was it? Oh, that fake chicken.

01:11:57.279 --> 01:11:58.547
The chicken royale specifically.

01:11:58.547 --> 01:12:01.150
It was the consistency of
the chicken, how it tasted.

01:12:01.150 --> 01:12:04.787
It just tasted off. It
tasted really weird.

01:12:04.787 --> 01:12:09.058
Like, my body was like, "Do
not swallow. Spit out now."

01:12:09.058 --> 01:12:12.294
So I feel like as a nugget
version, it would work.

01:12:12.294 --> 01:12:15.597
But as the chicken royale,

01:12:15.597 --> 01:12:16.932
didn't work. It's gotta go.

01:12:17.399 --> 01:12:19.234
A Brit and an American swap countries

01:12:19.234 --> 01:12:20.869
to try each other's Domino's.

01:12:20.869 --> 01:12:22.538
This is Food Wars.

01:12:25.240 --> 01:12:26.642
We're going to start by
comparing a menu item

01:12:26.642 --> 01:12:28.477
you can find in both the US and the UK

01:12:28.477 --> 01:12:30.112
to see if there are subtle differences.

01:12:30.112 --> 01:12:32.414
This is a US large cheese pizza.

01:12:32.414 --> 01:12:34.583
This is their largest size.

01:12:34.583 --> 01:12:36.952
Feels like it's a little
bit bigger than our medium.

01:12:36.952 --> 01:12:38.287
In terms of visual impressions,

01:12:38.287 --> 01:12:39.888
it looks pretty similar to a cheese pizza

01:12:39.888 --> 01:12:41.090
that I'd find in the UK.

01:12:41.090 --> 01:12:43.359
This is the large, not the extra-large,

01:12:43.359 --> 01:12:45.527
and honestly it looks
pretty much like the size

01:12:45.527 --> 01:12:47.629
that I would expect from
a large pizza in the UK.

01:12:47.629 --> 01:12:50.032
Otherwise, it looks pretty
similar in terms of the crust.

01:12:50.032 --> 01:12:51.700
Obviously a lot of cheese on that.

01:12:51.700 --> 01:12:52.868
You get these little, like, spots

01:12:52.868 --> 01:12:54.803
where the cheese kind
of caramelizes on top.

01:12:54.803 --> 01:12:57.606
Yeah, pretty much like
what I'm used to in the UK.

01:12:59.074 --> 01:13:00.342
It seems pretty close, actually.

01:13:00.342 --> 01:13:02.478
I can definitely tell
this is mozzarella cheese

01:13:02.478 --> 01:13:05.147
and not whatever weird pizza
cheese we have in the US.

01:13:05.147 --> 01:13:08.917
So yeah, this is like,
it's like a cleaner taste.

01:13:08.917 --> 01:13:10.119
I like this. This is good.

01:13:10.119 --> 01:13:11.453
Give it a try.

01:13:11.453 --> 01:13:13.322
I haven't had a Domino's in ages.

01:13:13.322 --> 01:13:15.157
It's also looking like
there's a pretty high

01:13:15.157 --> 01:13:16.792
cheese-to-sauce ratio on that.

01:13:16.792 --> 01:13:19.628
I feel like if you look at
the kind of cross-section,

01:13:19.628 --> 01:13:22.097
it's a lot of cheese
and not a ton of sauce.

01:13:25.701 --> 01:13:26.969
That's really not that bad.

01:13:26.969 --> 01:13:29.471
I have had some New York
slices while I've been here,

01:13:29.471 --> 01:13:31.373
and it's kind of
comparable to one of those.

01:13:31.373 --> 01:13:33.942
I feel like I might offend some
New Yorkers by saying that.

01:13:34.843 --> 01:13:36.245
There's a lot of, like, talks

01:13:36.245 --> 01:13:37.913
happening around the room right now.

01:13:37.913 --> 01:13:40.682
What I mean by that is I
think like in terms of the way

01:13:40.682 --> 01:13:42.718
that the cheese and the
sauce blends together,

01:13:42.718 --> 01:13:44.586
there's, like, less of a distinction

01:13:44.586 --> 01:13:45.788
between the cheese and the sauce.

01:13:45.788 --> 01:13:47.656
It kind of just all forms one mass,

01:13:47.656 --> 01:13:49.758
and in that regard I
feel like it's similar

01:13:49.758 --> 01:13:50.692
to a New York slice.

01:13:50.692 --> 01:13:52.127
There are some differences though.

01:13:52.127 --> 01:13:54.029
The crust on this is,
like, way less crispy

01:13:54.029 --> 01:13:56.832
than I have come to associate
with the New York slice.

01:13:56.832 --> 01:13:58.467
There's also maybe not
quite as much flavor

01:13:58.467 --> 01:14:01.003
as some of the slices that I've tried.

01:14:03.939 --> 01:14:06.875
Here's all the UK Domino's menu items

01:14:06.875 --> 01:14:08.544
I can't get in the US.

01:14:08.544 --> 01:14:10.612
And here are all the Domino's
menu items from the US

01:14:10.612 --> 01:14:12.414
which you can't find in the UK.

01:14:13.782 --> 01:14:17.519
You guys have exclusive dough options.

01:14:17.519 --> 01:14:19.221
I don't know about this one, guys.

01:14:20.355 --> 01:14:21.623
The Double Decadence.

01:14:21.623 --> 01:14:23.358
You got like a double-layer

01:14:25.027 --> 01:14:28.096
crust with like a garlicky
cheese in the middle there.

01:14:28.096 --> 01:14:32.768
Here in the UK, a garlic-and-herb
stuffed-crust pizza.

01:14:32.768 --> 01:14:34.636
This one also looks terrible.

01:14:34.636 --> 01:14:35.704
Then a crispy crust.

01:14:35.704 --> 01:14:38.006
This has to be half-priced,
or you're getting ripped off.

01:14:38.006 --> 01:14:39.241
What is this crust?

01:14:39.241 --> 01:14:40.843
Producer: It's Italian-style.

01:14:40.843 --> 01:14:42.044
What's Italian-style?

01:14:42.044 --> 01:14:44.947
Yeah, it's like, not as
thin, but it's still thinner.

01:14:44.947 --> 01:14:46.515
So man, you guys really get specific

01:14:46.515 --> 01:14:48.817
with the thickness of your crust.

01:14:48.817 --> 01:14:50.619
They want to dial that in, huh?

01:14:50.619 --> 01:14:52.287
Yeah, this, I'd be like,

01:14:52.287 --> 01:14:54.022
in America, this would be the thin crust.

01:14:54.022 --> 01:14:56.859
This would be like, yeah I
got the the thin one, right?

01:14:56.859 --> 01:15:00.095
And then this would be
like, people just rioting.

01:15:00.095 --> 01:15:01.930
Domino's in the US has crust options,

01:15:01.930 --> 01:15:03.465
which we don't have in the UK.

01:15:03.465 --> 01:15:05.334
We'll start with this one,
which is the pan crust.

01:15:05.334 --> 01:15:06.368
I mean, it looks pretty good.

01:15:06.368 --> 01:15:08.203
It is obviously much thicker

01:15:08.203 --> 01:15:10.472
than the standard hand-tossed slice was.

01:15:10.472 --> 01:15:14.142
You do get that kind of like
pan-crust bottom there as well.

01:15:16.845 --> 01:15:18.847
I like that you get more sauce

01:15:18.847 --> 01:15:20.682
and more distinct areas of sauce on this

01:15:20.682 --> 01:15:21.517
than the standard slice.

01:15:21.517 --> 01:15:22.351
I think often for me,

01:15:22.351 --> 01:15:24.386
the sauce is kind of the star of the show,

01:15:24.386 --> 01:15:26.855
especially when it's a fast-food pizza

01:15:26.855 --> 01:15:28.090
and the cheese generally doesn't have

01:15:28.090 --> 01:15:29.224
that much flavor to it.

01:15:29.224 --> 01:15:32.528
I will say I was expecting it
to be crispier on the bottom.

01:15:32.528 --> 01:15:35.430
When you see the kind of, like,
the cook marks on the bottom,

01:15:35.430 --> 01:15:37.099
I was expecting that to
be a nice, solid crust,

01:15:37.099 --> 01:15:39.067
but it is kind of squidgy.

01:15:39.067 --> 01:15:39.902
Not too bad.

01:15:39.902 --> 01:15:41.069
Let me try a little bit of crust.

01:15:44.172 --> 01:15:45.207
It's slightly crispier on the edge.

01:15:45.207 --> 01:15:47.342
Next up, we've got the Brooklyn crust.

01:15:47.342 --> 01:15:49.978
Now, I've already made
comparisons to New York slices,

01:15:49.978 --> 01:15:52.581
which have drawn some
criticism from the room.

01:15:52.581 --> 01:15:55.450
But this is supposed to
mimic a New York slice.

01:15:55.450 --> 01:15:57.352
As I now know from a New York slice,

01:15:57.352 --> 01:15:59.621
generally you're talking
low-moisture mozzarella,

01:15:59.621 --> 01:16:02.791
the sauce, and that kind
of mixture of like crispy,

01:16:02.791 --> 01:16:06.061
but a little bit floppy on the crust,

01:16:06.061 --> 01:16:08.096
which, kind of this is
doing, to be honest.

01:16:08.096 --> 01:16:11.033
So it sort of looks like a New York slice.

01:16:11.033 --> 01:16:12.367
But does it taste like one?

01:16:14.536 --> 01:16:15.637
No.

01:16:15.637 --> 01:16:17.039
No it doesn't.

01:16:17.039 --> 01:16:20.175
I'm sorry to the great state of New York

01:16:20.175 --> 01:16:22.277
for what Domino's has done to your pizzas.

01:16:24.513 --> 01:16:25.347
And then finally,

01:16:25.347 --> 01:16:27.049
Domino's in the US does
a gluten-free base.

01:16:27.049 --> 01:16:28.717
I don't know what they've
done to this gluten-free base.

01:16:28.717 --> 01:16:30.819
They've cut it so weirdly.

01:16:30.819 --> 01:16:32.888
Can you see the cross-sections on this?

01:16:32.888 --> 01:16:36.224
I think maybe they were
trying to do it into squares,

01:16:36.224 --> 01:16:37.793
but have just completely
messed up the angle.

01:16:37.793 --> 01:16:42.130
So now you get these like weird
kind of diamond-shaped slice

01:16:42.130 --> 01:16:45.901
in the middle, some like tiny
triangle ones on the sides.

01:16:45.901 --> 01:16:46.735
I don't know.

01:16:53.609 --> 01:16:55.577
Joe: Oh, man. Right?

01:16:55.577 --> 01:16:56.411
Oh man.

01:16:57.846 --> 01:16:58.680
No.

01:17:00.415 --> 01:17:01.583
That's bad.

01:17:01.583 --> 01:17:03.051
What have they done there?

01:17:03.051 --> 01:17:04.686
Yeah, that's a miss.

01:17:04.686 --> 01:17:07.289
I feel like if I were gluten-free,

01:17:08.223 --> 01:17:10.058
I think I might just skip Domino's.

01:17:10.058 --> 01:17:12.995
All right, let's go through these pizzas.

01:17:12.995 --> 01:17:17.299
Vegi Volcano, veggies and
jalapenos making it volcano-ey.

01:17:19.034 --> 01:17:20.435
Let's go, spice it up.

01:17:24.940 --> 01:17:26.842
You know, this is good.

01:17:27.976 --> 01:17:28.877
Off to a good start.

01:17:28.877 --> 01:17:32.047
The next veggie, the Veg-a-Roma.

01:17:32.047 --> 01:17:34.282
This one has, like, a
lot of seasoning on it.

01:17:34.282 --> 01:17:35.283
No.

01:17:35.283 --> 01:17:40.288
Here we got the, this just
says spicy, our hot and spicy.

01:17:40.422 --> 01:17:42.958
Not that spicy. I mean, I'm
seeing the jalapenos in here.

01:17:42.958 --> 01:17:45.227
That other one, the
volcano one was spicier.

01:17:45.227 --> 01:17:46.061
Tandoori hot.

01:17:46.061 --> 01:17:48.363
OK, I am excited for this. I'm for real.

01:17:48.363 --> 01:17:51.266
There's no tandoori
chicken pizza in the US.

01:17:51.266 --> 01:17:53.301
Yeah, that's good.

01:17:53.301 --> 01:17:54.302
That's good.

01:17:54.302 --> 01:17:55.137
I like that.

01:17:55.137 --> 01:17:56.371
Compared to other tandoori chicken,

01:17:56.371 --> 01:17:59.875
this probably is, like,
not even remotely good.

01:17:59.875 --> 01:18:03.011
But on the pizza, yeah,
that's a cool, that's like a,

01:18:04.146 --> 01:18:06.381
that's a nice flavor profile
combination they got there.

01:18:06.381 --> 01:18:07.649
Yeah, good on them for that one.

01:18:07.649 --> 01:18:08.483
Good job.

01:18:08.483 --> 01:18:10.786
So here are all the
Domino's premade pizzas

01:18:10.786 --> 01:18:13.388
I can get in the US which
you can't find in the UK.

01:18:13.388 --> 01:18:15.757
On like a sort of visual level,

01:18:15.757 --> 01:18:18.193
these look a lot busier
than I would expect

01:18:18.193 --> 01:18:21.129
a pizza in the UK to look.
Like, these things are topped.

01:18:21.129 --> 01:18:22.197
So we'll start with this one,

01:18:22.197 --> 01:18:25.367
which is the Philly cheesesteak pizza.

01:18:25.367 --> 01:18:27.602
Philly cheesesteak, an
iconic American food.

01:18:27.602 --> 01:18:28.437
I've never really had

01:18:28.437 --> 01:18:30.338
a proper American Philly
cheesesteak before.

01:18:30.338 --> 01:18:32.174
This is my introduction to them,

01:18:32.174 --> 01:18:33.308
which I'm sure the people of Philly

01:18:33.308 --> 01:18:34.543
will be thrilled to hear.

01:18:37.212 --> 01:18:38.914
It's very creamy, and I think the texture

01:18:38.914 --> 01:18:42.718
of the American cheese is a
bit like claggy in the mouth.

01:18:42.718 --> 01:18:44.019
I don't love the peppers.

01:18:44.019 --> 01:18:45.420
I feel like the peppers are
kind of overpowering it a lot.

01:18:45.420 --> 01:18:47.622
They've been really
generous with the peppers

01:18:47.622 --> 01:18:49.357
and not super generous with the steak.

01:18:49.357 --> 01:18:52.160
I feel like if you flip the
ratio of those toppings,

01:18:52.160 --> 01:18:53.862
this would be OK.

01:18:53.862 --> 01:18:56.698
Next up, we have the Wisconsin six-cheese.

01:18:56.698 --> 01:18:59.501
OK, so this is a very cheesy pizza.

01:18:59.501 --> 01:19:02.137
I'm told Wisconsin is known for its dairy

01:19:02.137 --> 01:19:03.939
and, I suppose, its cheese production.

01:19:07.242 --> 01:19:08.910
They've actually been quite
generous with the sauce

01:19:08.910 --> 01:19:10.045
under the cheese, which I like,

01:19:10.045 --> 01:19:13.181
because you need it to, like,
cut through all of that dairy.

01:19:13.181 --> 01:19:16.685
OK, the Vegi Supreme.

01:19:16.685 --> 01:19:19.087
Oh, no.

01:19:19.087 --> 01:19:21.723
Corn on pizza, no!

01:19:27.729 --> 01:19:29.965
Oh, God, I can really taste the corn.

01:19:29.965 --> 01:19:31.199
Meatilicious.

01:19:31.199 --> 01:19:32.534
Guys, come on.

01:19:32.534 --> 01:19:34.536
Oh, no!

01:19:34.536 --> 01:19:35.370
I'm realizing something,

01:19:35.370 --> 01:19:38.907
I do not have a taste for UK sausage.

01:19:39.741 --> 01:19:41.476
Whatever we've been
getting for these shoots.

01:19:41.476 --> 01:19:43.612
I think because your
guys' is pork and beef,

01:19:43.612 --> 01:19:44.613
like the way you're spicing it,

01:19:44.613 --> 01:19:45.714
there's something about it.

01:19:45.714 --> 01:19:48.917
I get it why you guys would
like it. You grew up eating it.

01:19:48.917 --> 01:19:51.853
We'll get Harry a sausage
when he comes to the US,

01:19:51.853 --> 01:19:53.054
and you'll see what I mean.

01:19:53.054 --> 01:19:54.956
Maybe it's a different type of sausage

01:19:54.956 --> 01:19:55.957
and we just name it something different,

01:19:55.957 --> 01:20:00.095
but this sausage you guys have is weird.

01:20:00.095 --> 01:20:01.530
Oh, yeah.

01:20:01.530 --> 01:20:02.597
Texas.

01:20:02.597 --> 01:20:03.665
I see the barbecue.

01:20:03.665 --> 01:20:05.767
Besides that, why else is this Texas?

01:20:05.767 --> 01:20:10.739
I see chicken, I see a few
sparse slices of bacon or ham.

01:20:11.139 --> 01:20:13.909
Yeah, all this stuff is in Texas.

01:20:13.909 --> 01:20:18.246
This does not represent the
state of Texas in any way.

01:20:18.246 --> 01:20:20.582
Next up, we have the ExtravaganZZa.

01:20:20.582 --> 01:20:24.085
This one I think is
probably the most chaotic

01:20:24.085 --> 01:20:25.187
in terms of toppings.

01:20:25.187 --> 01:20:26.054
What have we even got on here?

01:20:26.054 --> 01:20:28.423
I'm seeing ham,

01:20:28.423 --> 01:20:33.328
pepperoni, sausage, mushrooms, peppers,

01:20:33.328 --> 01:20:35.497
onions, and black olives?

01:20:35.497 --> 01:20:37.432
And I feel like I still might
have missed some things.

01:20:37.432 --> 01:20:39.334
I feel like I'm being
overloaded right now.

01:20:39.334 --> 01:20:40.602
You think you've kind of like identified

01:20:40.602 --> 01:20:41.436
what the flavor of it is,

01:20:41.436 --> 01:20:43.905
and then you bite down on
something else, and then suddenly

01:20:43.905 --> 01:20:45.307
you're tasting something
completely different.

01:20:45.307 --> 01:20:47.776
Next up is the Memphis barbecue pizza.

01:20:47.776 --> 01:20:49.878
Now, this one has the barbecue sauce base.

01:20:49.878 --> 01:20:51.279
I believe it does have provolone

01:20:51.279 --> 01:20:52.447
as well as mozzarella on it,

01:20:52.447 --> 01:20:54.749
which might explain some
of the extra cheesiness.

01:20:54.749 --> 01:20:57.452
And then you have some onions
and the grilled chicken.

01:21:00.021 --> 01:21:02.958
I know it is a sweet
barbecue sauce technically,

01:21:02.958 --> 01:21:04.359
and they are not kidding
when they say that,

01:21:04.359 --> 01:21:06.761
because this is a very, very sweet,

01:21:06.761 --> 01:21:08.630
very, very sweet barbecue sauce.

01:21:08.630 --> 01:21:10.665
And I think that does kind of overpower

01:21:10.665 --> 01:21:12.234
anything else that's going on.

01:21:12.234 --> 01:21:13.501
Mighty Meaty.

01:21:15.704 --> 01:21:17.939
OK, oh, yeah, this guy again.

01:21:19.574 --> 01:21:22.143
This has to be half-price or
you're getting ripped off.

01:21:22.143 --> 01:21:23.612
This thing.

01:21:23.612 --> 01:21:24.746
The cheeseburger pizza.

01:21:24.746 --> 01:21:27.015
The cheeseburger US
pizza I did really like.

01:21:28.516 --> 01:21:29.718
Burger sauce is on here?

01:21:30.652 --> 01:21:32.954
Yeah, I like this.

01:21:32.954 --> 01:21:33.822
It's good.

01:21:34.823 --> 01:21:36.324
I'm eating them on the pickles.

01:21:37.859 --> 01:21:40.662
Ladies and gentlemen, the Absolute Banger.

01:21:43.331 --> 01:21:45.200
What is absolutely banging about this?

01:21:45.200 --> 01:21:46.668
OK, one, two.

01:21:48.803 --> 01:21:50.205
Three.

01:21:50.205 --> 01:21:52.340
Just bringing it all to the front, guys.

01:21:52.340 --> 01:21:53.174
One bite.

01:21:55.944 --> 01:21:57.879
I don't know if it's really banger.

01:21:57.879 --> 01:21:59.681
Next up we have the deluxe pizza.

01:21:59.681 --> 01:22:01.750
This looks like a slightly
less chaotic version

01:22:01.750 --> 01:22:02.984
of the ExtravaganZZa.

01:22:02.984 --> 01:22:04.986
There's still like a
lot of toppings on here,

01:22:04.986 --> 01:22:05.954
but not quite so many.

01:22:05.954 --> 01:22:08.490
It's not like piled high
like the ExtravaganZZa was.

01:22:08.490 --> 01:22:10.025
See if it tastes any less chaotic

01:22:10.025 --> 01:22:12.827
than its slightly more packed-out cousin.

01:22:16.164 --> 01:22:18.266
What I'm realizing is I don't
really like peppers on pizza.

01:22:18.266 --> 01:22:20.402
I feel like it's quite a strong flavor,

01:22:20.402 --> 01:22:22.904
and when you get a fast-food
pizza specifically,

01:22:22.904 --> 01:22:25.373
where most of the toppings
and the cheese and the sauce

01:22:25.373 --> 01:22:27.208
don't really offer that
much in terms of taste,

01:22:27.208 --> 01:22:28.043
I feel like you have to be quite careful

01:22:28.043 --> 01:22:28.877
with your flavor balance.

01:22:28.877 --> 01:22:30.712
And peppers are kind of
throwing that off for me.

01:22:30.712 --> 01:22:33.181
Next up we have the Cali
chicken bacon ranch.

01:22:33.181 --> 01:22:35.750
So this one has chicken,
bacon, diced tomatoes,

01:22:35.750 --> 01:22:38.119
I believe our old friend
provolone is back again,

01:22:38.119 --> 01:22:40.422
and, of course, there
is ranch on this pizza.

01:22:45.694 --> 01:22:47.195
You can see the ranch.

01:22:47.195 --> 01:22:50.365
So it's basically the ranch
in lieu of tomato sauce

01:22:50.365 --> 01:22:51.199
on the bottom.

01:22:51.199 --> 01:22:53.435
I still think I just prefer
tomato sauce on a pizza.

01:22:53.435 --> 01:22:55.537
I don't think I will be
swapping out my pizza sauce

01:22:55.537 --> 01:22:57.505
for ranch anytime soon at home.

01:22:57.505 --> 01:22:59.641
Good lord, guys, no!

01:22:59.641 --> 01:23:01.109
I'm going to try a meatball.

01:23:01.109 --> 01:23:03.778
Could someone intelligent
in the comments explain

01:23:03.778 --> 01:23:05.480
the difference between
US sausage and meatballs

01:23:05.480 --> 01:23:06.881
and UK sausage and meatballs?

01:23:06.881 --> 01:23:08.850
It's just, it's notably different.

01:23:19.060 --> 01:23:20.662
The Meateor.

01:23:20.662 --> 01:23:22.897
Too much. Too much.

01:23:22.897 --> 01:23:25.033
Vegi Sizzler?

01:23:28.269 --> 01:23:31.272
It's spicy. It's sizzling.

01:23:31.272 --> 01:23:32.741
I know this is weird to say this,

01:23:32.741 --> 01:23:36.244
but is it unfair or
cheating to market something

01:23:36.244 --> 01:23:37.879
as being really sizzling and spicy

01:23:37.879 --> 01:23:41.483
if all you're doing is dumping
jalapenos on it, right?

01:23:41.483 --> 01:23:42.951
I don't think they did anything to, like,

01:23:42.951 --> 01:23:44.619
it's not like a spicy sauce.

01:23:44.619 --> 01:23:46.021
They didn't add like
any other spices to it

01:23:46.021 --> 01:23:46.855
from what I can tell.

01:23:46.855 --> 01:23:48.656
They just loaded it with jalapenos,

01:23:48.656 --> 01:23:50.558
which is like, well, right,

01:23:50.558 --> 01:23:53.128
but a little more effort than that, guys.

01:23:53.128 --> 01:23:54.329
New Yorker, what?

01:23:55.230 --> 01:23:57.465
I feel like I've seen this before.

01:23:57.465 --> 01:23:58.299
Producer: You did.

01:23:58.299 --> 01:24:01.102
No, in the past five minutes.

01:24:03.938 --> 01:24:06.708
Next up is the spinach feta pizza.

01:24:06.708 --> 01:24:08.109
I think I'll stick to my spanokopita

01:24:08.109 --> 01:24:11.246
instead of my spinach and feta pizza.

01:24:11.246 --> 01:24:13.648
This is the Buffalo chicken pizza.

01:24:13.648 --> 01:24:17.519
We have chicken, onions, and
quite a lot of Buffalo sauce.

01:24:20.155 --> 01:24:21.756
That's barely even a pizza.

01:24:21.756 --> 01:24:23.591
I don't know if you can call that a pizza.

01:24:23.591 --> 01:24:27.595
Oh, no, it's the breakfast
brickie! Or the Brekkie?

01:24:27.595 --> 01:24:29.697
Oh, look what it did to the box.

01:24:31.566 --> 01:24:32.400
What is on it?

01:24:32.400 --> 01:24:36.571
OK, I'm seeing mushrooms,
the sausage, ham,

01:24:36.571 --> 01:24:39.240
tomatoes, and HP sauce.

01:24:41.276 --> 01:24:43.778
I think people would get this
as a novelty and then realize

01:24:43.778 --> 01:24:46.714
that the jokes on them when it shows up.

01:24:46.714 --> 01:24:49.951
Here we go with the vegan Margherita.

01:24:54.622 --> 01:24:57.125
They were generous with the herbs,

01:24:57.125 --> 01:24:59.627
whatever, the extra herbs.
They're generous with that,

01:24:59.627 --> 01:25:01.930
which is code for this has no taste.

01:25:06.768 --> 01:25:07.969
Tuna Supreme.

01:25:09.370 --> 01:25:12.073
Oh, God, it looks like cat food.

01:25:12.073 --> 01:25:15.910
Tuna on pizza is horrifying.

01:25:15.910 --> 01:25:19.214
I see no Venn diagram of
enjoyment of those two flavors.

01:25:19.214 --> 01:25:20.982
Two completely separate circles.

01:25:20.982 --> 01:25:22.951
I feel like every alley cat's going to try

01:25:22.951 --> 01:25:25.220
and like break in here through the window.

01:25:33.328 --> 01:25:35.663
Oh, you people are insane.

01:25:35.663 --> 01:25:38.533
This whole island, maniacs.

01:25:38.533 --> 01:25:40.268
Oh, give me, I've got
to eat anything else.

01:25:40.268 --> 01:25:41.102
The taste in my mouth.

01:25:41.102 --> 01:25:42.103
What's the next one?

01:25:43.104 --> 01:25:44.539
I don't even care what it is.

01:25:46.407 --> 01:25:47.976
Chicken Feast.

01:25:49.310 --> 01:25:51.713
Oh, with the corn!

01:25:51.713 --> 01:25:53.081
That's good, anything else.

01:25:55.483 --> 01:25:56.317
Yeah, yeah.

01:25:56.317 --> 01:25:57.452
If you want to sell more
Chicken Feast pizzas,

01:25:57.452 --> 01:25:59.154
just give away free tuna pizzas.

01:26:00.188 --> 01:26:01.656
And then people are like, I
got this taste in my mouth.

01:26:01.656 --> 01:26:05.326
It's like, it'll cost
you, got it right here.

01:26:06.461 --> 01:26:09.330
Yeah, you're going to move
a lot of Chicken Feasts.

01:26:10.865 --> 01:26:13.468
Next up, we have the Pacific veggie pizza.

01:26:13.468 --> 01:26:15.003
Not sure what makes this Pacific.

01:26:15.003 --> 01:26:17.805
Are these veggies
exclusive to the Pacific?

01:26:17.805 --> 01:26:18.640
Because as far as I can tell,

01:26:18.640 --> 01:26:22.577
there's mushroom, onion,
olive, tomato, spinach?

01:26:27.015 --> 01:26:27.849
It's OK.

01:26:27.849 --> 01:26:29.117
Having eaten several pizzas in a row

01:26:29.117 --> 01:26:31.219
that contain meat in some form or other,

01:26:31.219 --> 01:26:32.787
I was quite looking
forward to a veggie one,

01:26:32.787 --> 01:26:35.490
hoping it would be a bit
lighter, but it kind of isn't.

01:26:35.490 --> 01:26:38.159
And then finally the last specialty pizza

01:26:38.159 --> 01:26:41.229
on the Domino's US menu is the MeatZZa.

01:26:41.229 --> 01:26:43.264
Having just gone from a veggie-only pizza,

01:26:43.264 --> 01:26:45.333
now I'm going to a meat-only pizza.

01:26:45.333 --> 01:26:49.871
This one has bacon, ham,
pepperoni, and sausage.

01:26:53.074 --> 01:26:55.009
There's something about American meat.

01:26:56.010 --> 01:26:58.313
But I think it's just
generally a lot saltier

01:26:58.313 --> 01:27:00.014
than what we're used to in the UK.

01:27:00.848 --> 01:27:01.749
As I was chewing that,

01:27:01.749 --> 01:27:04.852
I could just feel my
mouth like drying out.

01:27:04.852 --> 01:27:06.688
I think generally my
takeaway from this section

01:27:06.688 --> 01:27:08.856
is you guys need to
just calm down slightly,

01:27:08.856 --> 01:27:10.425
because this is too much.

01:27:10.425 --> 01:27:13.928
All right, we got here reduced-fat cheese,

01:27:13.928 --> 01:27:17.498
which I've been told is on
the UK or the UK-only pizza.

01:27:17.498 --> 01:27:19.000
Oh, you.

01:27:21.769 --> 01:27:23.972
OK, I don't know what to show you.

01:27:23.972 --> 01:27:25.139
I mean, it looks like cheese.

01:27:25.139 --> 01:27:27.542
And then vegan cheese.

01:27:27.542 --> 01:27:31.646
But it comes with its own
garlic-and-herb dip, vegan.

01:27:31.646 --> 01:27:33.648
Let's see what the vegan's got going on.

01:27:37.085 --> 01:27:38.152
It tastes sour.

01:27:38.152 --> 01:27:41.055
Sauce options you only get in
the UK, starting over here,

01:27:41.055 --> 01:27:42.624
just a straight barbecue sauce.

01:27:42.624 --> 01:27:45.526
We have honey barbecue,
they have regular barbecue.

01:27:45.526 --> 01:27:50.531
And then over here, this
monstrosity has sun-dried tomatoes

01:27:50.798 --> 01:27:53.034
and garlic sauce.

01:27:53.034 --> 01:27:56.904
They have four exclusive
meat toppings here in the UK.

01:27:56.904 --> 01:27:58.806
Hotdog slice is unreal.

01:27:58.806 --> 01:28:00.675
Chorizo sausage, sounds nice.

01:28:00.675 --> 01:28:02.477
Pork meatballs.

01:28:02.477 --> 01:28:05.046
Tandoori chicken, yeah,
that sounds real good.

01:28:05.046 --> 01:28:08.283
They also have two meatless meat options,

01:28:08.283 --> 01:28:13.288
vegan soya strips and vegan
soya-and-wheat pepperoni.

01:28:15.023 --> 01:28:16.324
I think we saw that earlier.

01:28:16.324 --> 01:28:19.260
They have seven nonmeat topping options.

01:28:19.260 --> 01:28:23.264
Sweet corn, Domino's herbs,
burger sauce, gherkins,

01:28:23.264 --> 01:28:26.734
Heinz ketchup, HP sauce,
and garlic spread.

01:28:26.734 --> 01:28:29.203
Here it is, the UK-only.

01:28:29.203 --> 01:28:33.308
It looks like an alien
community opened a pizza place,

01:28:33.308 --> 01:28:35.943
and they were like, here's
that pizza you like.

01:28:35.943 --> 01:28:37.478
Like, this is all things humans like,

01:28:37.478 --> 01:28:38.780
and all together like this.

01:28:38.780 --> 01:28:41.316
Like, the completely
fundamental misunderstanding

01:28:41.316 --> 01:28:42.450
of how food works.

01:28:46.888 --> 01:28:48.222
That was really bad.

01:28:48.222 --> 01:28:50.191
Now, beyond the premade specialty pizzas,

01:28:50.191 --> 01:28:52.860
they have some individual
toppings and customization options

01:28:52.860 --> 01:28:54.696
in the US which we can't find in the UK.

01:28:54.696 --> 01:28:57.899
So Joe has kindly taken a bunch
of the exclusive US toppings

01:28:57.899 --> 01:29:01.336
and added them to one
pizza to create a US only.

01:29:01.336 --> 01:29:03.104
I don't even know what he's put on here.

01:29:03.104 --> 01:29:04.238
The crust looks weird.

01:29:04.238 --> 01:29:06.808
I think he's gone thin
crust, banana peppers,

01:29:06.808 --> 01:29:08.309
spinach is back on there.

01:29:09.243 --> 01:29:11.512
This looks like a meat of some kind,

01:29:11.512 --> 01:29:14.048
but I can't tell you which one.

01:29:14.048 --> 01:29:15.383
Is that like beef?

01:29:15.383 --> 01:29:17.051
The steak from the Philly cheesesteak.

01:29:17.051 --> 01:29:19.520
The base sauce has been swapped
out for ranch of course.

01:29:19.520 --> 01:29:22.190
A little extra of that and light cheese.

01:29:22.190 --> 01:29:25.693
I mean, this thing looks
like a bit of a disaster.

01:29:30.598 --> 01:29:33.167
Look how thin that is.

01:29:33.167 --> 01:29:34.869
What have you done, man?

01:29:34.869 --> 01:29:36.037
Oh, that's bad.

01:29:36.871 --> 01:29:39.273
Domino's in the UK also has its own sides

01:29:39.273 --> 01:29:42.877
that I haven't had ever,
so why not try them now?

01:29:42.877 --> 01:29:43.911
Starting over here.

01:29:45.313 --> 01:29:46.247
Potato wedges.

01:29:47.682 --> 01:29:49.183
Oh, they have fries, whatever.

01:29:51.452 --> 01:29:52.854
Yep, not bad.

01:29:52.854 --> 01:29:54.122
Chicken strippers.

01:29:56.190 --> 01:29:57.058
Stripping it up.

01:29:59.827 --> 01:30:00.661
Just OK.

01:30:00.661 --> 01:30:02.964
I mean, the pizza's usually amazing,

01:30:02.964 --> 01:30:04.899
so I don't know why you
get chicken strips or fries

01:30:04.899 --> 01:30:06.300
at a pizza place.

01:30:06.300 --> 01:30:07.869
Oh, the nachos.

01:30:07.869 --> 01:30:08.669
No!

01:30:09.937 --> 01:30:11.372
Oh, no!

01:30:11.372 --> 01:30:13.741
UK, what have you done?

01:30:13.741 --> 01:30:16.010
If you want to be a millionaire,

01:30:16.010 --> 01:30:19.747
open a decent Mexican
restaurant in London.

01:30:19.747 --> 01:30:20.948
You're not going to try very hard.

01:30:20.948 --> 01:30:25.520
Just above horrible, two or three steps.

01:30:25.520 --> 01:30:27.355
The line will be out the door.

01:30:27.355 --> 01:30:29.857
Oh, my God, my soul hurts.

01:30:29.857 --> 01:30:32.059
This is so terrible.

01:30:32.059 --> 01:30:33.995
Then we're onto some
exclusive US side options

01:30:33.995 --> 01:30:35.163
we can't find in the UK.

01:30:35.163 --> 01:30:36.564
Firstly, we have tater tots.

01:30:36.564 --> 01:30:37.398
Now, if I'm correct,

01:30:37.398 --> 01:30:39.567
these are basically balls
of like mashed potato,

01:30:39.567 --> 01:30:40.401
which are then fried.

01:30:40.401 --> 01:30:42.170
They can then be topped
with a range of things.

01:30:42.170 --> 01:30:44.839
The ones we've got here are
Philly cheesesteak tots.

01:30:48.342 --> 01:30:49.177
Not bad.

01:30:49.177 --> 01:30:50.678
There could be like slightly
more flavor going on.

01:30:50.678 --> 01:30:52.914
Then we have two stuffed
cheesy bread options.

01:30:52.914 --> 01:30:54.816
As the name suggests, these
are big pieces of bread

01:30:54.816 --> 01:30:57.285
topped with lots of cheese
and a filling of your choice.

01:30:57.285 --> 01:31:00.321
Here we have a
spinach-and-feta cheesy bread,

01:31:00.321 --> 01:31:04.258
and then I believe this one is
bacon jalapeno cheesy bread.

01:31:04.258 --> 01:31:06.260
Then we have two twist options.

01:31:06.260 --> 01:31:08.963
Here we have some garlic bread twists

01:31:08.963 --> 01:31:11.265
and Parmesan bread twists.

01:31:11.265 --> 01:31:12.567
Now, you don't eat the twist on their own,

01:31:12.567 --> 01:31:14.302
because they come with dips.

01:31:14.302 --> 01:31:17.738
So this is a cheesy marinara dip.

01:31:17.738 --> 01:31:20.241
It's basically just a bowl
of their marinara sauce

01:31:20.241 --> 01:31:22.443
with lots of melted cheese on top.

01:31:22.443 --> 01:31:24.545
I kind of see the appeal of
dipping these in marinara sauce.

01:31:24.545 --> 01:31:26.447
I don't know if it needs the cheese.

01:31:26.447 --> 01:31:27.582
That's such overkill.

01:31:30.451 --> 01:31:32.887
I would enjoy that way more
if it was just marinara sauce.

01:31:32.887 --> 01:31:35.790
In addition to the cheesy
marinara sauce option,

01:31:35.790 --> 01:31:38.092
there's also a five-cheese dip.

01:31:38.092 --> 01:31:39.427
That's just pure oil.

01:31:40.561 --> 01:31:42.029
Vegan nuggets?

01:31:42.029 --> 01:31:44.398
Ooh, I don't like this.

01:31:44.398 --> 01:31:45.233
No.

01:31:46.234 --> 01:31:48.336
Twisted dough balls.

01:31:48.336 --> 01:31:49.837
I bet that was better when it was hot.

01:31:49.837 --> 01:31:52.807
Again, why are you getting
this instead of pizza?

01:31:52.807 --> 01:31:54.075
Because it's the elements of pizza.

01:31:54.075 --> 01:31:55.977
These are the Chicken Kickers.

01:31:55.977 --> 01:31:57.078
Prepare for that kick.

01:31:59.013 --> 01:32:00.147
And I don't think it's coming.

01:32:00.147 --> 01:32:01.849
To be honest, this slaw
looks a little rough,

01:32:01.849 --> 01:32:04.585
but you can get a real
big tub of coleslaw.

01:32:04.585 --> 01:32:05.620
We're still talking about sides,

01:32:05.620 --> 01:32:06.888
but now we're onto chicken.

01:32:06.888 --> 01:32:08.723
Domino's in the US has some wing options,

01:32:08.723 --> 01:32:10.291
which we can't find in the UK.

01:32:10.291 --> 01:32:11.359
We'll start with these ones here,

01:32:11.359 --> 01:32:13.694
which are garlic Parmesan wings.

01:32:13.694 --> 01:32:15.997
They have not skimped on
the garlic parm sauce,

01:32:15.997 --> 01:32:18.466
although I will say these are tiny wings.

01:32:19.567 --> 01:32:20.735
What chicken has this come off?

01:32:20.735 --> 01:32:22.570
This is the world's smallest chicken.

01:32:25.339 --> 01:32:27.508
Maybe one of the worst
wings I've ever had.

01:32:28.509 --> 01:32:30.778
The sauce is like a weird, gloopy texture,

01:32:30.778 --> 01:32:32.513
which I really do not appreciate.

01:32:32.513 --> 01:32:33.814
It doesn't even taste nice.

01:32:33.814 --> 01:32:34.982
And the other wing option we got today

01:32:34.982 --> 01:32:36.951
was sweet mango habanero.

01:32:36.951 --> 01:32:38.019
I'll give these a quick try.

01:32:38.019 --> 01:32:40.288
The bar is pretty low after
those garlic parm wings,

01:32:40.288 --> 01:32:41.122
I have to say.

01:32:41.122 --> 01:32:42.456
It's definitely better than the other one.

01:32:42.456 --> 01:32:44.225
The sauce actually tastes kind of nice.

01:32:44.225 --> 01:32:45.459
A little bit of tweaking your method

01:32:45.459 --> 01:32:46.627
I think would go a long way, Domino's,

01:32:46.627 --> 01:32:49.297
so please fix this, because
these are not very good.

01:32:49.297 --> 01:32:52.266
Domino's in the US also
has boneless wings.

01:32:52.266 --> 01:32:54.502
I'm still not exactly sure
what counts as a boneless wing

01:32:54.502 --> 01:32:57.038
versus a nugget, but they're
calling these boneless wings.

01:32:57.038 --> 01:32:58.105
We've got two options today,

01:32:58.105 --> 01:33:01.676
which are the crispy
bacon and buffalo chicken.

01:33:01.676 --> 01:33:03.811
I'll have a quick bite
of the crispy bacon.

01:33:05.112 --> 01:33:06.681
These have been disappointing.

01:33:06.681 --> 01:33:08.316
I thought Americans did
wings better than this,

01:33:08.316 --> 01:33:09.250
I'm going to be honest.

01:33:09.250 --> 01:33:10.284
There are two other boneless wings,

01:33:10.284 --> 01:33:13.487
which are a sweet barbecue
bacon and a spicy jalapeno,

01:33:13.487 --> 01:33:14.889
but we didn't get those today.

01:33:14.889 --> 01:33:17.358
Domino's in the US also
offers a range of sandwiches

01:33:17.358 --> 01:33:18.326
and pastas.

01:33:18.326 --> 01:33:21.095
I don't why, because
they all look real bad.

01:33:21.095 --> 01:33:22.096
I'll work my way down this way,

01:33:22.096 --> 01:33:25.333
starting with the Italian
sandwich, a chicken parm,

01:33:25.333 --> 01:33:27.668
and once again, a Philly cheesesteak.

01:33:27.668 --> 01:33:31.238
Although I feel like if you
tried to sell this in Philly,

01:33:31.238 --> 01:33:32.239
they would run you out of town.

01:33:32.239 --> 01:33:33.874
There are some other
sandwiches we didn't get today,

01:33:33.874 --> 01:33:37.044
including a Buffalo
chicken, a chicken habanero,

01:33:37.044 --> 01:33:39.981
a Mediterranean veggie,
and a chicken bacon ranch.

01:33:39.981 --> 01:33:41.515
Then we're onto the pasta options.

01:33:41.515 --> 01:33:44.518
The ones I have in front of
me today are a chicken Alfredo

01:33:44.518 --> 01:33:46.988
and a pasta primavera.

01:33:46.988 --> 01:33:48.689
I'm going to be honest,
after trying all the pizzas,

01:33:48.689 --> 01:33:51.192
I am not going to try these
for the sake of my health.

01:33:51.192 --> 01:33:53.561
I've heard from Joe that
they're all terrible.

01:33:53.561 --> 01:33:56.631
I think the pastas at Domino's

01:33:56.631 --> 01:33:58.833
are an absolute abomination.

01:33:58.833 --> 01:34:00.635
And looking at them, I believe him.

01:34:00.635 --> 01:34:01.636
All right.

01:34:01.636 --> 01:34:06.641
♪ It's time for sauce
talk foreign exchange ♪

01:34:09.343 --> 01:34:10.478
Sauce talk.

01:34:10.478 --> 01:34:11.312
Thank you.

01:34:11.312 --> 01:34:12.213
Garlic-and-herb dip.

01:34:13.114 --> 01:34:15.516
This isn't ranch, but it's pretty close.

01:34:15.516 --> 01:34:16.517
Oh, you have a vegan one.

01:34:16.517 --> 01:34:18.819
I can taste the difference, but
this one's pretty good, too.

01:34:18.819 --> 01:34:19.720
Honey mustard.

01:34:21.222 --> 01:34:22.657
I'm a big honey mustard guy.

01:34:22.657 --> 01:34:24.258
Wow, that's actually really good.

01:34:24.258 --> 01:34:25.660
Like your sauces are good.

01:34:25.660 --> 01:34:26.494
Tangy salsa.

01:34:26.494 --> 01:34:27.328
OK, I think this is where

01:34:27.328 --> 01:34:28.963
we're about to fall off a cliff here.

01:34:28.963 --> 01:34:30.598
There's no way you got salsa right.

01:34:30.598 --> 01:34:31.432
You know what it is?

01:34:31.432 --> 01:34:35.169
It's like here's tomato
sauce, here's salsa.

01:34:35.169 --> 01:34:37.538
You're like, you stopped like here.

01:34:37.538 --> 01:34:39.306
Oh, duh, Frank's.

01:34:39.306 --> 01:34:41.075
USA, baby, all the way from Jersey.

01:34:43.344 --> 01:34:44.812
Yep, that's Frank's.

01:34:44.812 --> 01:34:45.846
I don't know why I did that.

01:34:45.846 --> 01:34:47.148
There are four sauce options in the US

01:34:47.148 --> 01:34:48.482
which we don't have in the UK,

01:34:48.482 --> 01:34:52.086
and these are a marinara
sauce, a blue cheese sauce,

01:34:52.086 --> 01:34:55.256
ranch dressing, and a
sweet mango habanero.

01:34:55.256 --> 01:34:57.291
I will very quickly give these all a try.

01:34:59.827 --> 01:35:00.661
It's fine.

01:35:00.661 --> 01:35:03.097
The marinara sauce is very sweet.

01:35:03.097 --> 01:35:04.732
Blue cheese dressing.

01:35:05.666 --> 01:35:07.868
I like a little bit of
blue cheese on wings.

01:35:07.868 --> 01:35:09.270
It can be very overpowering.

01:35:15.509 --> 01:35:16.911
Oh, no, no, no.

01:35:16.911 --> 01:35:18.713
It's not even that it's
like too much blue cheese.

01:35:18.713 --> 01:35:21.916
It's just like there's some
kind of odd flavor in there.

01:35:21.916 --> 01:35:23.517
It does taste like slightly soured.

01:35:23.517 --> 01:35:25.252
Of course, we have the ranch.

01:35:25.252 --> 01:35:28.322
They put this on some of
their pizzas directly.

01:35:28.322 --> 01:35:30.024
And for the real ranch lovers,

01:35:30.024 --> 01:35:31.926
you can then also dip
your crust in it as well.

01:35:31.926 --> 01:35:35.029
I can't open this because my
hands are covered in grease.

01:35:35.029 --> 01:35:36.697
It's quite tangy.

01:35:36.697 --> 01:35:39.633
And last but not least,
the sweet mango habanero.

01:35:39.633 --> 01:35:41.502
I quite like this on the wings.

01:35:42.403 --> 01:35:45.039
I think this is like by far the best

01:35:45.039 --> 01:35:48.075
and, like, most well-balanced
of any of these sauces.

01:35:48.075 --> 01:35:50.578
It looks like for desserts
you guys got cookies.

01:35:53.581 --> 01:35:54.682
OK.

01:35:54.682 --> 01:35:56.050
And what's this last one?

01:35:56.050 --> 01:35:57.885
Oh, God, what the hell is this?

01:35:57.885 --> 01:35:59.820
What do I even do with it?

01:35:59.820 --> 01:36:00.654
Do I cut it?

01:36:00.654 --> 01:36:01.822
Do I just bite right into it?

01:36:03.657 --> 01:36:06.527
Listen to me, from what I can tell,

01:36:06.527 --> 01:36:09.964
it's just pizza dough with
melted chocolate on it.

01:36:09.964 --> 01:36:11.499
No effort on this.

01:36:11.499 --> 01:36:12.333
Yeah, it's weird.

01:36:12.333 --> 01:36:13.634
Then the US has some dessert options

01:36:13.634 --> 01:36:15.202
which we can't find in the UK.

01:36:15.202 --> 01:36:18.205
Over here we have chocolate lava cake.

01:36:18.205 --> 01:36:22.676
OK, no there is, yeah,
there is some lava in there.

01:36:22.676 --> 01:36:24.678
But it's still very gooey on the inside.

01:36:26.213 --> 01:36:27.214
Not bad.

01:36:27.214 --> 01:36:29.650
Next up we have some
cinnamon bread twists.

01:36:29.650 --> 01:36:31.218
So I think it's basically
just the same dough

01:36:31.218 --> 01:36:33.788
that they use for the garlic
or Parmesan bread twists,

01:36:33.788 --> 01:36:35.222
but instead of topping
them with savory things,

01:36:35.222 --> 01:36:36.457
they top them with cinnamon

01:36:36.457 --> 01:36:38.793
and then give you some
sweet icing for dipping.

01:36:41.028 --> 01:36:42.696
This is really good.

01:36:42.696 --> 01:36:45.466
We don't have a lot of like cinnamon roll,

01:36:45.466 --> 01:36:47.935
Cinnabon-type of stuff in the UK,

01:36:47.935 --> 01:36:48.969
which I think is a travesty,

01:36:48.969 --> 01:36:50.905
because I think it's really tasty.

01:36:50.905 --> 01:36:52.239
And honestly, yeah, these are pretty good.

01:36:52.239 --> 01:36:54.375
And then last, but by no means least,

01:36:54.375 --> 01:36:56.343
we have the marbled cookie brownie.

01:36:56.343 --> 01:36:59.713
I feel like Domino's are like
surprisingly good at desserts.

01:36:59.713 --> 01:37:00.714
It's really not bad.

01:37:03.617 --> 01:37:05.686
I think overall, I have to
say I'm kind of disappointed

01:37:05.686 --> 01:37:06.720
by the US Domino's menu.

01:37:06.720 --> 01:37:10.157
I was expecting some good
flavors, some good textures,

01:37:10.157 --> 01:37:11.358
and various bits and bobs,

01:37:11.358 --> 01:37:13.060
but I really didn't get much of that.

01:37:13.060 --> 01:37:14.595
Honestly, my main takeaway

01:37:14.595 --> 01:37:16.897
is that I didn't like most of the menu.

01:37:16.897 --> 01:37:17.932
This might be controversial

01:37:17.932 --> 01:37:19.366
considering how much I hate vegetables,

01:37:19.366 --> 01:37:22.703
but of all like the pizza pizzas,

01:37:22.703 --> 01:37:24.138
or like predetermined ones,

01:37:24.138 --> 01:37:26.707
I was actually very impressed
with the volcano veggie,

01:37:26.707 --> 01:37:28.242
er, Vegi Volcano.

01:37:28.242 --> 01:37:29.276
That's like really good.

01:37:29.276 --> 01:37:30.144
That was earlier.

01:37:30.144 --> 01:37:32.112
I was a little more
optimistic to be honest,

01:37:32.112 --> 01:37:33.547
but I was surprised by
how much I liked it.

01:37:33.547 --> 01:37:34.648
So yeah, that was a good one.

01:37:34.648 --> 01:37:36.116
This sounds kind of ridiculous to say,

01:37:36.116 --> 01:37:38.519
but I think if I had to take
one menu item from the US

01:37:38.519 --> 01:37:40.354
and bring it back with me to the UK,

01:37:40.354 --> 01:37:42.323
I'd probably take the
cinnamon bread twists.

01:37:42.323 --> 01:37:43.624
Well, if I had to pick one,

01:37:43.624 --> 01:37:45.025
probably the one that
almost made me throw up,

01:37:45.025 --> 01:37:45.860
that'd be the tuna.

01:37:45.860 --> 01:37:46.694
It was so bad.

01:37:47.728 --> 01:37:48.629
Horrifying.

01:37:49.463 --> 01:37:50.698
Like I'm glad I know.

01:37:51.532 --> 01:37:53.067
But that was, I mean, it
almost made me throw up.

01:37:53.067 --> 01:37:54.301
Of the things on the US menu,

01:37:54.301 --> 01:37:57.037
I think the one that I would
delete permanently if I could,

01:37:57.037 --> 01:37:58.739
would actually be the ExtravaganZZa.

01:37:58.739 --> 01:37:59.940
I kind of said it at the time,

01:37:59.940 --> 01:38:02.109
but I think it's just
far too many toppings.

01:38:02.109 --> 01:38:03.477
I think Joe agrees with me on this one,

01:38:03.477 --> 01:38:05.112
so I hope he doesn't push back too hard.

01:38:05.112 --> 01:38:06.847
But I think the more toppings you add,

01:38:06.847 --> 01:38:08.949
the kind of worse you
end up making a pizza.

01:38:08.949 --> 01:38:12.386
There was not a square centimeter
of cheese on that pizza.

01:38:12.386 --> 01:38:14.555
It was just toppings, toppings, toppings.

01:38:14.555 --> 01:38:16.056
Flavors were all over the place.

01:38:16.056 --> 01:38:18.092
It didn't know what pizza
it was trying to be.

01:38:18.092 --> 01:38:20.094
It was just a disaster, far too much.

01:38:20.094 --> 01:38:20.928
Dial it back, guys.

01:38:20.928 --> 01:38:22.029
Calm down.

